{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589287407,"sessionID":"ses_e2a25640effei5XE2iy7zBxs56","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5db6287001fX8T1rNXrc2mu4","sessionID":"ses_e2a25640effei5XE2iy7zBxs56","messageID":"msg_1d5db5378001anwlWnjE4y9w0w","type":"tool","id":"call_17a5e7de75044b7a82a195ef","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml, lines 1-131\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SHIPPED INSTRUCTION EMBED (INTERACTIVE, ONE REPOSITORY)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Careful operator bringing one repository's root instruction file up to the shipped template without losing a line the repository wrote\n5: purpose: Compose in memory, print the plan with its digest, ask once, write only after that yes and only against the digest the plan printed, then prove on disk that nothing was dropped and hand back the engine's own undo block\n6: action: Read the engine and the target -> run the plan -> show the plan, the diff, the budget and the digest -> explicit yes -> apply with that digest -> re-read the written files through the check engine -> print the engine's undo block\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: sequential_read_plan_confirmed_embed\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: interactive\n16:   approvals: explicit_yes\n17:   dry_run: print_the_plan_then_status_ok_without_asking\n18:   tracking: one_repository_root\n19:   validation: re_read_the_written_files_through_the_check_engine\n20:   never_commit: true\n21: \n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES\n24: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n25: mutation_boundaries:\n26:   read_only: false\n27:   allowed_targets:\n28:     - \"AGENTS.md, the root document: created when the repository has none, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block, and left alone when it already matches\"\n29:     - \"CLAUDE.md, folded into the block and replaced by a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer by default. Kept as it is, with its lines still moved into the block, when --keep-claude-md was given. Created as that pointer when it is absent and the run writes another file.\"\n30:     - \".codex/AGENTS.md, folded into the block and removed\"\n31:     - \".cursor/rules/repo-local.md, the generated mirror of a non-empty block; removed when the block is empty\"\n32:     - \".cursor/rules/skill-routing.md, rewritten by its own generator, sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, which this engine calls and never composes a byte of\"\n33:     - \"REPO RULES.md, the router: shipped rows that are missing are appended and no other row is touched, and a missing file is created only behind --create-router\"\n34:     - \"the backup directory the plan prints, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ or the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path: every path the run touches is copied there before the first write, and the record beside the copies is what restore reads\"\n35:   forbidden_targets:\n36:     - \"any path outside that allowlist, which the engine checks in code before every write rather than trusting this document\"\n37:     - \".skilled/**, which /doctor:update owns, including the manifest this engine reads\"\n38:     - \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs and its lib/, which own the composition and never change here\"\n39:     - \"a rule file a REPO RULES.md row points at, which is authored through the create-repo-rule route and never by this one\"\n40:     - \"the git index, history and remotes\"\n41:   invariant: \"Nothing is written until the plan has printed its digest and the operator has answered yes to that plan. The plan call composes in memory and writes nothing, the apply refuses a digest that no longer matches and writes nothing in that case, and every path the run touches is copied to the backup before the first byte. The proof that no repository line was dropped runs against the bytes now on disk, and a violation restores from the backup automatically. A no at the question ends the run with STATUS=CANCELLED and nothing written.\"\n42: \n43: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n44: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n45: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n46: upstream_assets:\n47:   embed_engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs\"\n48:   check_engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs\"\n49:   section_library: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/lib/agents-md-sections.cjs\"\n50:   template_manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\"\n51:   pointer_generator: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, called by the engine and never by this workflow\"\n52:   repo_rules_checker: \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-repo-rule/scripts/check-repo-rules.cjs, called by the engine after a router write\"\n53:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\"\n54: \n55: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: # INPUTS\n57: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n58: inputs:\n59:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n60:   root: \"The repository to compose for when --root <dir> is passed, resolved by the engine (default none, so the repository this command ships in).\"\n61:   dry_run: \"--dry-run prints the plan and its digest, then STATUS=OK without asking a question (default false). The plan call writes nothing either way; the flag only removes the question and the write.\"\n62:   plan_digest: \"The plan digest the plan printed. It is what makes the approved bytes checkable: the apply recomposes and refuses any digest that no longer matches.\"\n63:   digest_confirmation: \"true once the operator has answered yes to the plan whose digest was on screen. A plan approved at one tree is never applied at another, because the digest would not match.\"\n64:   keep_claude_md: \"--keep-claude-md folds a divergent CLAUDE.md into the block and keeps the file. --remove-claude-md folds it and leaves a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer, which is the default (default false, so the pointer).\"\n65:   create_router: \"--create-router creates REPO RULES.md from the shipped rows when it is missing (default false, so a missing router is a note and a finding).\"\n66: \n67: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n68: # WORKFLOW\n69: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n70: workflow:\n71:   phase_1_read:\n72:     purpose: \"Load what the run is built from before anything is composed or asked\"\n73:     activities:\n74:       - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/lib/agents-md-sections.cjs and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json exist. If any is missing, report the missing path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. An embed without its engine or its manifest would invent a template.\"\n75:       - \"Read the engine's interface before driving it: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs with no subcommand prints its usage block and exits 2, and that block is the whole list of calls this workflow may make. plan composes in memory and writes nothing. apply --plan-digest <digest> refuses a digest that does not match the composition and otherwise backs up, writes and proves. restore --run=<dir> puts back the paths one apply recorded. --dry-run prints a plan and writes nothing. --yes takes the confirmation as given.\"\n76:       - \"Read .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt for the plan, question, refusal and result wording. Every visible line comes from there.\"\n77:       - \"Read nothing out of the target to decide the composition. The three-way section classification, the block and the budget are the engine's answers, and a second reading here would be a second opinion that drifts from it.\"\n78: \n79:   phase_2_plan:\n80:     purpose: \"Run the read-only plan and keep its notes, its findings and its digest apart\"\n81:     activities:\n82:       - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs plan, adding --root \\\"{root}\\\" when the operator passed one, --keep-claude-md when the divergent copy is to be kept, --create-router when a missing router is to be created, and --dry-run when the operator asked for one. The plan call writes nothing: it composes every target in memory, prints each target with its action, the diff, the new block, the budget, the survival ledger, the backup folder and the plan digest.\"\n83:       - \"Keep the engine's exact lines: the target list with the action each target takes, absent included, each note, each diff, the block lines between the engine's `block:` and `block-end:` markers, the budget line, each finding line, the preservation line, the backup line, the backup-fallback line when one prints, the undo line and the plan-digest line. They are what the operator approves, and no other plan is ever the one this run applies.\"\n84:       - \"Exit 0 with NOTHING TO DO means the repository is already in its target state, which the engine prints without a plan. Render the presentation contract's unchanged result with the engine's own notes, ask nothing, write nothing and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK.\"\n85:       - \"A finding line that says the composed document is past the byte ceiling is a finding rather than a refusal: every carried line is kept, because preservation outranks the budget. Show it with the plan and let the operator decide. A run whose composition drops a line refuses instead, exits 1 and writes nothing; print the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL and stop.\"\n86:       - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own lines, print the dry-run line and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing and writes nothing, so it runs no question and no apply.\"\n87:       - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document, a symlinked REPO RULES.md or Cursor mirror the run would write, or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n88: \n89:   phase_3_approval:\n90:     purpose: \"Ask the one embed question against the plan on screen, and write only after its yes\"\n91:     activities:\n92:       - \"Ask the embed question once, in the presentation contract's wording, naming the files the plan will create, replace or remove, the backup folder, the router rows the plan would add and the plan digest. The operator answers about the plan the operator has just read, which is this run's plan.\"\n93:       - \"Any answer other than yes is a no: print the cancelled result naming the declined embed, state Changed: none, and end with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled. Nothing is written.\"\n94:       - \"Never default an answer, never carry an approval from an earlier run, and never accept a digest the operator has not seen. Phase 4 runs only after this phase's yes.\"\n95: \n96:   phase_4_write:\n97:     purpose: \"Write the approved composition and nothing else, only after the embed yes\"\n98:     activities:\n99:       - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs apply --plan-digest \\\"{plan_digest}\\\" with exactly the flags the plan ran with: --root \\\"{root}\\\" when it was given, --keep-claude-md or --remove-claude-md as approved, and --create-router when it was approved. Run it only after the embed yes.\"\n100:       - \"Exit 2 with a message that the plan digest does not match the composition now means the tree changed after the plan, so nothing was written. Quote the engine's message, offer the plan again against the current tree, and end with STATUS=FAIL. Never retry the apply with a recomposed digest of your own: the point of the digest is that the approved bytes are the written bytes.\"\n101:       - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n102:       - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n103:       - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line or a `foreign:` line. The engine restored from the backup by itself unless it printed `nothing was restored`, and kept the backup. Quote the lines the proof named, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it when the restore ran. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n104:       - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\"\n105:       - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n106: \n107:   phase_5_reread:\n108:     purpose: \"Prove the written repository reads back through the read-only engine\"\n109:     activities:\n110:       - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs once, with --root \\\"{root}\\\" when this run was pointed at another repository, and read the twelve rows against the plan's claims: the block the plan composed is the block on disk, and the paths the apply printed as written are the paths the check reads.\"\n111:       - \"The engine prints its own check-after line at the end of a successful apply. Keep that line and the re-read beside each other: two readings of the same tree disagreeing is a failure, not a warning.\"\n112:       - \"A row that still reports FINDING after a clean write is not a failed embed: the write completed and the row names a different requirement, so report it as the next step and keep the result at STATUS=OK.\"\n113:       - \"When the re-read cannot run at all, report its message, keep the write result, and name the missing check as the next step. Never report an embed as verified when the re-read never answered.\"\n114: \n115:   phase_6_report:\n116:     purpose: \"Summarize the run and hand the way back to the operator\"\n117:     activities:\n118:       - \"When the write ran and read back, render the presentation contract's embedded result with the paths the engine wrote or removed, the pointer-sync and repo-rules lines as they printed, the backup folder, the re-read verdict, the undo block the engine printed and the next line those lines name.\"\n119:       - \"Print the engine's undo block exactly as the apply printed it: its Undo: line, the restore command it names and the copy line per overwritten file, in that order and with no path shortened. Never compose an undo of this route's own and never run it here. Never run the undo inside this route.\"\n120:       - \"A no answered a question: render the cancelled result naming what was declined, state Changed: none and end with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled.\"\n121:       - \"A dry run: render the dry-run result with the plan, the digest and the dry-run line, and end with STATUS=OK.\"\n122:       - \"NOTHING TO DO: render the unchanged result with the engine's notes and STATUS=OK.\"\n123:       - \"A refusal, a missing asset, a dropped line or a digest mismatch stopped the run: render the failure result naming the phase and the engine's code, with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n124:       - \"End by saying the operator commits the written files themselves; this route stages and commits nothing.\"\n125: \n126: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n127: # OUTPUT\n128: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n129: output:\n130:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\"\n131:   statuses: [OK, CANCELLED, FAIL]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml, lines 1-131\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SHIPPED INSTRUCTION EMBED (INTERACTIVE, ONE REPOSITORY)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Careful operator bringing one repository's root instruction file up to the shipped template without losing a line the repository wrote\n5: purpose: Compose in memory, print the plan with its digest, ask once, write only after that yes and only against the digest the plan printed, then prove on disk that nothing was dropped and hand back the engine's own undo block\n6: action: Read the engine and the target -> run the plan -> show the plan, the diff, the budget and the digest -> explicit yes -> apply with that digest -> re-read the written files through the check engine -> print the engine's undo block\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: sequential_read_plan_confirmed_embed\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: interactive\n16:   approvals: explicit_yes\n17:   dry_run: print_the_plan_then_status_ok_without_asking\n18:   tracking: one_repository_root\n19:   validation: re_read_the_written_files_through_the_check_engine\n20:   never_commit: true\n21: \n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES\n24: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n25: mutation_boundaries:\n26:   read_only: false\n27:   allowed_targets:\n28:     - \"AGENTS.md, the root document: created when the repository has none, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block, and left alone when it already matches\"\n29:     - \"CLAUDE.md, folded into the block and replaced by a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer by default. Kept as it is, with its lines still moved into the block, when --keep-claude-md was given. Created as that pointer when it is absent and the run writes another file.\"\n30:     - \".codex/AGENTS.md, folded into the block and removed\"\n31:     - \".cursor/rules/repo-local.md, the generated mirror of a non-empty block; removed when the block is empty\"\n32:     - \".cursor/rules/skill-routing.md, rewritten by its own generator, sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, which this engine calls and never composes a byte of\"\n33:     - \"REPO RULES.md, the router: shipped rows that are missing are appended and no other row is touched, and a missing file is created only behind --create-router\"\n34:     - \"the backup directory the plan prints, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ or the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path: every path the run touches is copied there before the first write, and the record beside the copies is what restore reads\"\n35:   forbidden_targets:\n36:     - \"any path outside that allowlist, which the engine checks in code before every write rather than trusting this document\"\n37:     - \".skilled/**, which /doctor:update owns, including the manifest this engine reads\"\n38:     - \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs and its lib/, which own the composition and never change here\"\n39:     - \"a rule file a REPO RULES.md row points at, which is authored through the create-repo-rule route and never by this one\"\n40:     - \"the git index, history and remotes\"\n41:   invariant: \"Nothing is written until the plan has printed its digest and the operator has answered yes to that plan. The plan call composes in memory and writes nothing, the apply refuses a digest that no longer matches and writes nothing in that case, and every path the run touches is copied to the backup before the first byte. The proof that no repository line was dropped runs against the bytes now on disk, and a violation restores from the backup automatically. A no at the question ends the run with STATUS=CANCELLED and nothing written.\"\n42: \n43: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n44: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n45: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n46: upstream_assets:\n47:   embed_engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs\"\n48:   check_engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs\"\n49:   section_library: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/lib/agents-md-sections.cjs\"\n50:   template_manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\"\n51:   pointer_generator: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, called by the engine and never by this workflow\"\n52:   repo_rules_checker: \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-repo-rule/scripts/check-repo-rules.cjs, called by the engine after a router write\"\n53:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\"\n54: \n55: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: # INPUTS\n57: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n58: inputs:\n59:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n60:   root: \"The repository to compose for when --root <dir> is passed, resolved by the engine (default none, so the repository this command ships in).\"\n61:   dry_run: \"--dry-run prints the plan and its digest, then STATUS=OK without asking a question (default false). The plan call writes nothing either way; the flag only removes the question and the write.\"\n62:   plan_digest: \"The plan digest the plan printed. It is what makes the approved bytes checkable: the apply recomposes and refuses any digest that no longer matches.\"\n63:   digest_confirmation: \"true once the operator has answered yes to the plan whose digest was on screen. A plan approved at one tree is never applied at another, because the digest would not match.\"\n64:   keep_claude_md: \"--keep-claude-md folds a divergent CLAUDE.md into the block and keeps the file. --remove-claude-md folds it and leaves a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer, which is the default (default false, so the pointer).\"\n65:   create_router: \"--create-router creates REPO RULES.md from the shipped rows when it is missing (default false, so a missing router is a note and a finding).\"\n66: \n67: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n68: # WORKFLOW\n69: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n70: workflow:\n71:   phase_1_read:\n72:     purpose: \"Load what the run is built from before anything is composed or asked\"\n73:     activities:\n74:       - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/lib/agents-md-sections.cjs and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json exist. If any is missing, report the missing path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. An embed without its engine or its manifest would invent a template.\"\n75:       - \"Read the engine's interface before driving it: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs with no subcommand prints its usage block and exits 2, and that block is the whole list of calls this workflow may make. plan composes in memory and writes nothing. apply --plan-digest <digest> refuses a digest that does not match the composition and otherwise backs up, writes and proves. restore --run=<dir> puts back the paths one apply recorded. --dry-run prints a plan and writes nothing. --yes takes the confirmation as given.\"\n76:       - \"Read .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt for the plan, question, refusal and result wording. Every visible line comes from there.\"\n77:       - \"Read nothing out of the target to decide the composition. The three-way section classification, the block and the budget are the engine's answers, and a second reading here would be a second opinion that drifts from it.\"\n78: \n79:   phase_2_plan:\n80:     purpose: \"Run the read-only plan and keep its notes, its findings and its digest apart\"\n81:     activities:\n82:       - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs plan, adding --root \\\"{root}\\\" when the operator passed one, --keep-claude-md when the divergent copy is to be kept, --create-router when a missing router is to be created, and --dry-run when the operator asked for one. The plan call writes nothing: it composes every target in memory, prints each target with its action, the diff, the new block, the budget, the survival ledger, the backup folder and the plan digest.\"\n83:       - \"Keep the engine's exact lines: the target list with the action each target takes, absent included, each note, each diff, the block lines between the engine's `block:` and `block-end:` markers, the budget line, each finding line, the preservation line, the backup line, the backup-fallback line when one prints, the undo line and the plan-digest line. They are what the operator approves, and no other plan is ever the one this run applies.\"\n84:       - \"Exit 0 with NOTHING TO DO means the repository is already in its target state, which the engine prints without a plan. Render the presentation contract's unchanged result with the engine's own notes, ask nothing, write nothing and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK.\"\n85:       - \"A finding line that says the composed document is past the byte ceiling is a finding rather than a refusal: every carried line is kept, because preservation outranks the budget. Show it with the plan and let the operator decide. A run whose composition drops a line refuses instead, exits 1 and writes nothing; print the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL and stop.\"\n86:       - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own lines, print the dry-run line and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing and writes nothing, so it runs no question and no apply.\"\n87:       - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document, a symlinked REPO RULES.md or Cursor mirror the run would write, or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n88: \n89:   phase_3_approval:\n90:     purpose: \"Ask the one embed question against the plan on screen, and write only after its yes\"\n91:     activities:\n92:       - \"Ask the embed question once, in the presentation contract's wording, naming the files the plan will create, replace or remove, the backup folder, the router rows the plan would add and the plan digest. The operator answers about the plan the operator has just read, which is this run's plan.\"\n93:       - \"Any answer other than yes is a no: print the cancelled result naming the declined embed, state Changed: none, and end with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled. Nothing is written.\"\n94:       - \"Never default an answer, never carry an approval from an earlier run, and never accept a digest the operator has not seen. Phase 4 runs only after this phase's yes.\"\n95: \n96:   phase_4_write:\n97:     purpose: \"Write the approved composition and nothing else, only after the embed yes\"\n98:     activities:\n99:       - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs apply --plan-digest \\\"{plan_digest}\\\" with exactly the flags the plan ran with: --root \\\"{root}\\\" when it was given, --keep-claude-md or --remove-claude-md as approved, and --create-router when it was approved. Run it only after the embed yes.\"\n100:       - \"Exit 2 with a message that the plan digest does not match the composition now means the tree changed after the plan, so nothing was written. Quote the engine's message, offer the plan again against the current tree, and end with STATUS=FAIL. Never retry the apply with a recomposed digest of your own: the point of the digest is that the approved bytes are the written bytes.\"\n101:       - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n102:       - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n103:       - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line or a `foreign:` line. The engine restored from the backup by itself unless it printed `nothing was restored`, and kept the backup. Quote the lines the proof named, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it when the restore ran. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n104:       - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\"\n105:       - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n106: \n107:   phase_5_reread:\n108:     purpose: \"Prove the written repository reads back through the read-only engine\"\n109:     activities:\n110:       - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs once, with --root \\\"{root}\\\" when this run was pointed at another repository, and read the twelve rows against the plan's claims: the block the plan composed is the block on disk, and the paths the apply printed as written are the paths the check reads.\"\n111:       - \"The engine prints its own check-after line at the end of a successful apply. Keep that line and the re-read beside each other: two readings of the same tree disagreeing is a failure, not a warning.\"\n112:       - \"A row that still reports FINDING after a clean write is not a failed embed: the write completed and the row names a different requirement, so report it as the next step and keep the result at STATUS=OK.\"\n113:       - \"When the re-read cannot run at all, report its message, keep the write result, and name the missing check as the next step. Never report an embed as verified when the re-read never answered.\"\n114: \n115:   phase_6_report:\n116:     purpose: \"Summarize the run and hand the way back to the operator\"\n117:     activities:\n118:       - \"When the write ran and read back, render the presentation contract's embedded result with the paths the engine wrote or removed, the pointer-sync and repo-rules lines as they printed, the backup folder, the re-read verdict, the undo block the engine printed and the next line those lines name.\"\n119:       - \"Print the engine's undo block exactly as the apply printed it: its Undo: line, the restore command it names and the copy line per overwritten file, in that order and with no path shortened. Never compose an undo of this route's own and never run it here. Never run the undo inside this route.\"\n120:       - \"A no answered a question: render the cancelled result naming what was declined, state Changed: none and end with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled.\"\n121:       - \"A dry run: render the dry-run result with the plan, the digest and the dry-run line, and end with STATUS=OK.\"\n122:       - \"NOTHING TO DO: render the unchanged result with the engine's notes and STATUS=OK.\"\n123:       - \"A refusal, a missing asset, a dropped line or a digest mismatch stopped the run: render the failure result naming the phase and the engine's code, with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n124:       - \"End by saying the operator commits the written files themselves; this route stages and commits nothing.\"\n125: \n126: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n127: # OUTPUT\n128: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n129: output:\n130:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\"\n131:   statuses: [OK, CANCELLED, FAIL]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794589287047,"end":1794589287407}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589287414,"sessionID":"ses_e2a25640effei5XE2iy7zBxs56","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5db60dc002H4Pm4rUhlPTGIb","sessionID":"ses_e2a25640effei5XE2iy7zBxs56","messageID":"msg_1d5db5378001anwlWnjE4y9w0w","type":"tool","id":"call_f318c46897f24711954aca9a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs, lines 1-823\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3: // MODULE: Doctor Agents-MD Contract Tests\n4: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: // Holds /doctor:agents-md together: the three routes in the manifest, the router,\n8: // the presentation contract, the three workflows and the command contract must\n9: // agree on the targets, the mutation classes, the asset paths, the engines they\n10: // name and the order a write happens in.\n11: //\n12: // The route validator checks structure and the engines' own suites check the bytes\n13: // they produce. What nothing else can see is the promise between the two: that the\n14: // writing workflow is shaped as plan, digest, yes and only then a write, that a no\n15: // leaves the tree exactly as it was, that the workflow's allowlist is the engine's\n16: // own list rather than a second one that drifts from it, and that the router stays\n17: // a router. This suite asserts those promises by reading the files.\n18: \n19: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n20: // 1. IMPORTS AND FIXTURES\n21: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n22: \n23: const assert = require('node:assert/strict');\n24: const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n25: const fs = require('node:fs');\n26: const os = require('node:os');\n27: const path = require('node:path');\n28: const test = require('node:test');\n29: const { parse: parseYaml } = require('yaml');\n30: \n31: const { composeFixture } = require('./fixtures/agents-md/compose-fixture.cjs');\n32: \n33: const DOCTOR = path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..');\n34: const ASSETS = path.join(DOCTOR, 'assets');\n35: const SCRIPTS = path.join(DOCTOR, 'scripts');\n36: const COMMANDS = path.resolve(DOCTOR, '..');\n37: const SKILL_DOC_ASSETS = path.resolve(DOCTOR, '..', '..', 'skills', 'sk-doc', 'sk-create-command', 'assets');\n38: \n39: const read = (file) => fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n40: \n41: const MANIFEST = parseYaml(read(path.join(DOCTOR, '_routes.yaml')));\n42: const ROUTES = MANIFEST.routes.filter((route) => route.command === '/doctor:agents-md');\n43: const routeFor = (target) => ROUTES.find((route) => route.target === target);\n44: \n45: const ROUTER = read(path.join(DOCTOR, 'agents-md.md'));\n46: const PRESENTATION = read(path.join(ASSETS, 'doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt'));\n47: const CHECK_YAML = read(path.join(ASSETS, 'doctor-agents-md-check.yaml'));\n48: const EMBED_YAML = read(path.join(ASSETS, 'doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml'));\n49: const RESTORE_YAML = read(path.join(ASSETS, 'doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml'));\n50: const SETUP_PRESENTATION = read(path.join(ASSETS, 'doctor-setup-presentation.txt'));\n51: const UPDATE_PRESENTATION = read(path.join(ASSETS, 'doctor-update-presentation.txt'));\n52: const CATALOG = read(path.join(COMMANDS, 'README.txt'));\n53: \n54: const CONTRACT = JSON.parse(read(path.join(SKILL_DOC_ASSETS, 'command-contract.json')));\n55: const SCHEMA = JSON.parse(read(path.join(SKILL_DOC_ASSETS, 'command-contract.schema.json')));\n56: const DOCTOR_CONTRACT = CONTRACT.families.doctor;\n57: const FAMILY_SCHEMA = SCHEMA.definitions.familyContract;\n58: \n59: const CHECK_ENGINE = '.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs';\n60: const EMBED_ENGINE = '.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs';\n61: const HELPER = path.join(SCRIPTS, 'doctor-helper-match.cjs');\n62: const EMBED_SCRIPT = path.join(SCRIPTS, 'agents-md-embed.cjs');\n63: \n64: // The engine's own write boundary, read from the engine. A second copy in the\n65: // workflow is the drift this suite exists to catch, so the allowlist cases compare\n66: // against this list rather than against a literal here.\n67: const { ALLOWLIST } = require(path.join(SCRIPTS, 'agents-md-embed.cjs'));\n68: \n69: const engineOf = (entry) => entry.match(/\\.skilled\\/\\S+\\.cjs/)[0];\n70: \n71: const CHECK_WORKFLOW = parseYaml(CHECK_YAML);\n72: const EMBED_WORKFLOW = parseYaml(EMBED_YAML);\n73: const RESTORE_WORKFLOW = parseYaml(RESTORE_YAML);\n74: const EMBED_PHASES = Object.keys(EMBED_WORKFLOW.workflow);\n75: const RESTORE_PHASES = Object.keys(RESTORE_WORKFLOW.workflow);\n76: \n77: const yamlStrings = (node, out = []) => {\n78:   if (Array.isArray(node)) {\n79:     for (const value of node) yamlStrings(value, out);\n80:   } else if (node && typeof node === 'object') {\n81:     for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(node)) {\n82:       out.push(key);\n83:       yamlStrings(value, out);\n84:     }\n85:   } else if (typeof node === 'string') {\n86:     out.push(node);\n87:   }\n88:   return out;\n89: };\n90: \n91: const phaseText = (workflow, phase) => yamlStrings(workflow.workflow[phase]).join('\\n');\n92: \n93: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n94: // 2. THE ROUTES\n95: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n96: \n97: test('the manifest holds a check, an embed and a restore route, and only check answers the bare command', () => {\n98:   assert.deepEqual(ROUTES.map((route) => route.target), ['check', 'embed', 'restore']);\n99:   // Three targets make the command multi-target, so the read-only one has to claim\n100:   // the bare invocation: without the flag a typed /doctor:agents-md would reach no\n101:   // bridge at all, and a bare invocation must never reach a route that writes.\n102:   assert.equal(routeFor('check').default_target, true);\n103:   assert.equal(routeFor('embed').default_target, undefined);\n104:   assert.equal(routeFor('restore').default_target, undefined);\n105:   assert.equal(routeFor('check').mutating, 'read-only');\n106:   assert.match(routeFor('check').gate3_location, /^n\\/a/);\n107:   assert.equal(routeFor('embed').mutating, 'mutates');\n108:   assert.equal(routeFor('restore').mutating, 'mutates');\n109:   for (const route of ROUTES) {\n110:     assert.equal(route.yaml, `doctor-agents-md-${route.target}.yaml`);\n111:     assert.ok(fs.existsSync(path.join(ASSETS, route.yaml)), route.yaml);\n112:     assert.deepEqual(route.mcp_tools, []);\n113:   }\n114:   assert.deepEqual(routeFor('check').allowed_flags, ['--json', '--root <dir>']);\n115:   assert.deepEqual([...routeFor('embed').allowed_flags].sort(), [\n116:     '--create-router',\n117:     '--dry-run',\n118:     '--keep-claude-md',\n119:     '--plan-digest <digest>',\n120:     '--remove-claude-md',\n121:     '--root <dir>',\n122:   ].sort());\n123:   assert.deepEqual([...routeFor('restore').allowed_flags].sort(), ['--dry-run', '--run <dir>', '--yes'].sort());\n124: });\n125: \n126: // The header is the file's own table of contents, and a reader who trusts it misses every\n127: // router it omits. The count is the folder's, so a new router file fails here until the\n128: // header names it.\n129: test('the route manifest header lists every router file in the folder', () => {\n130:   const header = read(path.join(DOCTOR, '_routes.yaml')).split(/^schema_version:/m)[0];\n131:   const listed = [...header.matchAll(/^#   \\/doctor:(\\S+)\\s+\\S+\\.md$/gm)].map((match) => match[1]).sort();\n132:   const routers = fs.readdirSync(DOCTOR)\n133:     .filter((file) => file.endsWith('.md') && !file.startsWith('local-'))\n134:     .map((file) => file.replace(/\\.md$/, ''))\n135:     .sort();\n136:   assert.deepEqual(listed, routers, 'the header names every router or the count in it is wrong');\n137: });\n138: \n139: test('the writing routes name every place the engines write and nothing else', () => {\n140:   const embed = routeFor('embed').gate3_location;\n141:   // Exactly the six allowlisted paths, the backup that makes the write reversible and\n142:   // the digest that decides whether the approved bytes are the bytes on disk.\n143:   for (const expected of [\n144:     /AGENTS\\.md/,\n145:     /CLAUDE\\.md/,\n146:     /\\.codex\\/AGENTS\\.md/,\n147:     /\\.cursor\\/rules\\/repo-local\\.md/,\n148:     /\\.cursor\\/rules\\/skill-routing\\.md/,\n149:     /REPO RULES\\.md/,\n150:     /backup/i,\n151:     /plan digest/i,\n152:   ]) {\n153:     assert.match(embed, expected);\n154:   }\n155:   // A release unit belongs to /doctor:update, and no embed run stages a commit.\n156:   assert.doesNotMatch(embed, /\\.skilled\\/skills|the git index|commit/i);\n157: \n158:   const restore = routeFor('restore').gate3_location;\n159:   assert.match(restore, /manifest\\.json/);\n160:   assert.match(restore, /allowlist/);\n161:   assert.match(restore, /recorded/);\n162: });\n163: \n164: test('every route names the engine calls its workflow runs and every trigger phrase carries three or more words', () => {\n165:   for (const route of ROUTES) {\n166:     for (const phrase of route.trigger_phrases) {\n167:       assert.ok(phrase.trim().split(/\\s+/).length >= 3, phrase);\n168:     }\n169:   }\n170:   // The check route reads, and only reads.\n171:   assert.deepEqual(routeFor('check').script_invocations.map(engineOf), [CHECK_ENGINE]);\n172: \n173:   // The plan writes nothing, the apply carries the digest the plan printed, and the\n174:   // re-read proves what landed. A plan call that already carried the digest would\n175:   // make the approval a formality, so it never does.\n176:   const embedCalls = routeFor('embed').script_invocations;\n177:   assert.deepEqual(embedCalls.map(engineOf), [EMBED_ENGINE, EMBED_ENGINE, CHECK_ENGINE]);\n178:   assert.match(embedCalls[0], /agents-md-embed\\.cjs plan/);\n179:   assert.doesNotMatch(embedCalls[0], /--plan-digest/);\n180:   assert.match(embedCalls[1], /agents-md-embed\\.cjs apply/);\n181:   assert.match(embedCalls[1], /--plan-digest <digest>/);\n182: \n183:   // The restore plan is the engine's own dry run, and the write repeats the record\n184:   // path the operator was shown.\n185:   const restoreCalls = routeFor('restore').script_invocations;\n186:   assert.deepEqual(restoreCalls.map(engineOf), [EMBED_ENGINE, EMBED_ENGINE, CHECK_ENGINE]);\n187:   assert.match(restoreCalls[0], /agents-md-embed\\.cjs restore --run=<dir> --dry-run/);\n188:   assert.match(restoreCalls[1], /agents-md-embed\\.cjs restore --run=<dir> --yes/);\n189:   assert.doesNotMatch(restoreCalls[0], /--yes/);\n190: });\n191: \n192: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n193: // 3. ROUTER AND PRESENTATION\n194: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n195: \n196: test('the router follows the router template: six canonical sections in order and no inline presentation', () => {\n197:   const headings = [...ROUTER.matchAll(/^## \\d+\\. ([A-Z ]+)$/gm)].map((match) => match[1]);\n198:   assert.deepEqual(headings, [\n199:     'ROUTER CONTRACT',\n200:     'OWNED ASSETS',\n201:     'MODE ROUTING',\n202:     'EXECUTION TARGETS',\n203:     'PRESENTATION BOUNDARY',\n204:     'WORKFLOW SUMMARY',\n205:   ]);\n206:   // A fenced block or a status line in the router would put a dashboard or a result\n207:   // template inline, where the presentation contract is the only place they belong.\n208:   assert.doesNotMatch(ROUTER, /```/);\n209:   assert.doesNotMatch(ROUTER, /STATUS=/);\n210: });\n211: \n212: test('the router frontmatter stays within budget and grants only the tools it uses', () => {\n213:   const description = ROUTER.match(/^description:\\s*\"(.*)\"$/m)[1];\n214:   assert.ok(description.length <= 110, `description is ${description.length} chars`);\n215:   assert.doesNotMatch(description, /[<>]/);\n216:   const hint = ROUTER.match(/^argument-hint:\\s*\"(.*)\"$/m)[1];\n217:   assert.ok(hint.length <= 140, `argument-hint is ${hint.length} chars`);\n218:   for (const token of ['[check|embed|restore]', '[--json]', '[--root <dir>]', '[--dry-run]', '[--plan-digest <digest>]', '[--run <dir>]', '[--yes]']) {\n219:     assert.ok(hint.includes(token), token);\n220:   }\n221:   const tools = ROUTER.match(/^allowed-tools:\\s*(.+)$/m)[1].split(',').map((tool) => tool.trim());\n222:   assert.deepEqual(tools, ['Read', 'Bash']);\n223:   // Instruction-document authoring is sk-doc's, so that is the one skill tag here.\n224:   assert.equal(ROUTER.split('<!-- skill_agent: system-skilled-doctor -->').length - 1, 1);\n225: });\n226: \n227: test('the router binds each target to the workflow asset its route names', () => {\n228:   for (const route of ROUTES) {\n229:     assert.match(\n230:       ROUTER,\n231:       new RegExp(`^\\\\| \\`${route.target}\\` \\\\| \\`\\\\.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/${route.yaml}\\` \\\\|$`, 'm'),\n232:       route.target,\n233:     );\n234:   }\n235: });\n236: \n237: test('the router names both engines as owned assets and composes nothing itself', () => {\n238:   const owned = ROUTER.split('## 2. OWNED ASSETS')[1].split('## 3.')[0];\n239:   assert.ok(owned.includes(CHECK_ENGINE), CHECK_ENGINE);\n240:   assert.ok(owned.includes(EMBED_ENGINE), EMBED_ENGINE);\n241:   assert.match(ROUTER, /Do not compose an `AGENTS\\.md` byte/);\n242: });\n243: \n244: test('the router resolves the bare command to check and keeps every write behind the digest and a yes', () => {\n245:   assert.match(ROUTER, /`default_target`/);\n246:   assert.match(ROUTER, /A bare `\\/doctor:agents-md` never reaches `embed` or `restore`, which write/);\n247:   assert.match(ROUTER, /never runs `apply` without the digest its own plan printed/);\n248:   assert.match(ROUTER, /never runs a writing target without its yes/);\n249: });\n250: \n251: test('the router step list runs the real order: plan, digest, yes, apply, re-read', () => {\n252:   const summary = ROUTER.split('## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY')[1];\n253:   const steps = summary.split('\\n').map((line) => line.trim()).filter((line) => /^\\d+\\. /.test(line));\n254:   const at = (pattern) => {\n255:     const index = steps.findIndex((step) => pattern.test(step));\n256:     assert.ok(index >= 0, `no step names ${pattern}`);\n257:     return index;\n258:   };\n259:   const plan = at(/agents-md-embed\\.cjs plan/);\n260:   const digest = at(/the plan digest/);\n261:   const question = at(/asks the embed question/);\n262:   const apply = at(/agents-md-embed\\.cjs apply --plan-digest/);\n263:   const reread = at(/re-reads the written repository/);\n264:   assert.ok(plan < digest, 'the plan is printed before its digest is offered');\n265:   assert.ok(digest < question, 'the digest is named before the question');\n266:   assert.ok(question < apply, 'the apply runs only after the question');\n267:   assert.ok(apply < reread, 'the re-read follows the write');\n268:   const stepText = steps.join('\\n');\n269:   assert.match(stepText, /ends the run as cancelled/);\n270:   assert.match(stepText, /nothing is written/);\n271:   assert.match(stepText, /restore/);\n272: });\n273: \n274: test('the presentation carries the menu, the accepted answers, the manifest rows and the valid targets line', () => {\n275:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^## 1\\. Argument Failure$/m);\n276:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^1\\) check$/m);\n277:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^2\\) embed$/m);\n278:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^3\\) restore$/m);\n279:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| `1` \\| target = `check` \\|/m);\n280:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| `2` \\| target = `embed` \\|/m);\n281:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| `3` \\| target = `restore` \\|/m);\n282:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^Valid targets: check, embed, restore$/m);\n283:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| `check` \\| `doctor-agents-md-check\\.yaml` \\| read-only \\|/m);\n284:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| `embed` \\| `doctor-agents-md-embed\\.yaml` \\| mutates \\|/m);\n285:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| `restore` \\| `doctor-agents-md-restore\\.yaml` \\| mutates \\|/m);\n286: });\n287: \n288: // A failure the router promises to catch has to have wording, or the agent invents one and\n289: // the operand hears a sentence the contract never approved. A value flag at the end of the\n290: // line and a second positional are the two an operator reaches by hand.\n291: test('the argument table defines a missing value and a second positional for every target', () => {\n292:   const table = PRESENTATION.split('## 1. Argument Failure')[1].split(/\\n## 2\\./u)[0];\n293:   const rows = table.split('\\n').filter((line) => line.startsWith('| '));\n294: \n295:   const missing = rows.find((line) => /value flag/u.test(line));\n296:   assert.ok(missing, 'no row for a value flag given without its value');\n297:   for (const flag of ['--plan-digest', '--root']) assert.ok(missing.includes(flag), `${flag} is not named`);\n298:   assert.match(missing, /STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"missing_argument\"/u);\n299:   assert.match(missing, /Try: /u);\n300: \n301:   const second = rows.find((line) => /second positional/u.test(line));\n302:   assert.ok(second, 'no row for a second positional');\n303:   // One suggestion per target, because the right next command differs by target.\n304:   assert.match(second, /\\/doctor:agents-md check \\[--json\\] \\[--root <dir>\\]/u);\n305:   assert.match(second, /\\/doctor:agents-md embed \\[--dry-run\\]/u);\n306:   assert.match(second, /\\/doctor:agents-md restore --run=<dir>/u);\n307:   assert.match(second, /STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"too_many_arguments\"/u);\n308: \n309:   // The router promises this table covers both cases, so it has to name them.\n310:   assert.match(ROUTER, /a value flag without its value/u);\n311:   assert.match(ROUTER, /a second positional/u);\n312: });\n313: \n314: // The engine has three outcomes for an exit 1 and the route has to mirror all three: a row\n315: // that could not be answered is not a finding, and reporting it as one sends the operator\n316: // looking for a fault that was never found.\n317: test('an unproven row ends the check as UNKNOWN, never as a finding', () => {\n318:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^Status: \\[OK\\|FINDINGS\\|UNKNOWN\\|ERROR\\]$/mu);\n319:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^STATUS=\\[OK\\|FINDINGS\\|UNKNOWN\\]$/mu);\n320:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /exit 1 with `findings=0` ends `STATUS=UNKNOWN`/u);\n321:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /never `STATUS=FINDINGS`/u);\n322:   const { output } = CHECK_WORKFLOW;\n323:   assert.match(output, /STATUS=UNKNOWN/u);\n324:   assert.match(output, /findings=0/u);\n325: });\n326: \n327: test('the presentation keeps the check table, the JSON passthrough and the digest it makes the operator approve', () => {\n328:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^Agents instruction check: \\[the root the engine read\\]$/m);\n329:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^DOCTOR TARGET UNCHANGED$/m);\n330:   assert.ok(PRESENTATION.includes(\"With `--json` print the engine's JSON and nothing else\"));\n331:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^Plan digest: \\[the engine's plan-digest line\\]$/m);\n332:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /Embed these files now\\? \\[yes\\/no\\]$/m);\n333:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /Restore these paths from that backup now\\? \\[yes\\/no\\]$/m);\n334:   // The digest is what the operator approves, so the wording has to say so.\n335:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /the digest on screen is the digest the apply repeats/);\n336:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /never compose a plan digest/);\n337: });\n338: \n339: test('the presentation closes on the unchanged, cancelled, dry-run, restored and failed templates', () => {\n340:   // Every status a route can print appears as its own line, because a workflow that\n341:   // ends on one of them must have been told the exact string.\n342:   for (const status of ['STATUS=OK', 'STATUS=FINDINGS', 'STATUS=UNKNOWN', 'STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled', 'STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"', 'STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"']) {\n343:     assert.match(PRESENTATION, new RegExp(`^${status.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, '\\\\$&')}$`, 'm'), status);\n344:   }\n345:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled$/m);\n346:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"\\[code\\]\"$/m);\n347:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"\\[message\\]\"$/m);\n348:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /Declined: \\[the embed \\| the restore\\]/);\n349:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next\\?`$/m);\n350: });\n351: \n352: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n353: // 4. THE CHECK WORKFLOW\n354: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n355: \n356: test('the check workflow is read-only and runs the check engine the route declares', () => {\n357:   assert.equal(CHECK_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.execution, 'read_only');\n358:   assert.equal(CHECK_WORKFLOW.mutation_boundaries.read_only, true);\n359:   assert.deepEqual(CHECK_WORKFLOW.mutation_boundaries.allowed_targets, []);\n360:   assert.ok(CHECK_YAML.includes(CHECK_ENGINE), CHECK_ENGINE);\n361: });\n362: \n363: test('the check workflow declares every variable its route resolves', () => {\n364:   for (const key of routeFor('check').setup_vars) {\n365:     assert.ok(key in CHECK_WORKFLOW.inputs, `inputs.${key} is missing`);\n366:   }\n367: });\n368: \n369: test('the check workflow passes --json and --root only when the operator asked', () => {\n370:   assert.match(CHECK_WORKFLOW.inputs.json_output, /true when --json is passed/);\n371:   assert.match(CHECK_YAML, /--json when the operator/);\n372:   assert.doesNotMatch(CHECK_YAML, /agents-md-check\\.cjs --json/);\n373:   assert.match(CHECK_WORKFLOW.inputs.root, /--root <dir>/);\n374:   // The default root is the repository the operator is in, so an unconditional\n375:   // --root would classify somebody else's tree.\n376:   assert.doesNotMatch(CHECK_YAML, /agents-md-check\\.cjs --root/);\n377: });\n378: \n379: test('the check workflow maps the engine exit classes to a route status', () => {\n380:   const { output } = CHECK_WORKFLOW;\n381:   assert.match(output, /STATUS=OK/);\n382:   assert.match(output, /STATUS=FINDINGS/);\n383:   // Exit 1 covers two outcomes, and the route has to keep them apart: a row nobody could\n384:   // answer is not a finding, and calling it one sends the operator after a fault that was\n385:   // never found.\n386:   assert.match(output, /STATUS=UNKNOWN/);\n387:   assert.match(output, /findings=0/);\n388:   assert.match(output, /STATUS=ERROR/);\n389: });\n390: \n391: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n392: // 5. THE EMBED AND RESTORE WORKFLOWS\n393: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n394: \n395: test('the embed workflow is interactive, writes only on a yes and never commits', () => {\n396:   assert.equal(EMBED_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.execution, 'interactive');\n397:   assert.equal(EMBED_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.approvals, 'explicit_yes');\n398:   assert.equal(EMBED_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.dry_run, 'print_the_plan_then_status_ok_without_asking');\n399:   assert.equal(EMBED_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.never_commit, true);\n400:   assert.deepEqual(EMBED_WORKFLOW.output.statuses, ['OK', 'CANCELLED', 'FAIL']);\n401:   assert.equal(EMBED_WORKFLOW.output.presentation, '.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt');\n402: });\n403: \n404: test('the embed workflow runs its phases in the read, plan, approval, write, re-read, report order', () => {\n405:   assert.deepEqual(EMBED_PHASES, [\n406:     'phase_1_read',\n407:     'phase_2_plan',\n408:     'phase_3_approval',\n409:     'phase_4_write',\n410:     'phase_5_reread',\n411:     'phase_6_report',\n412:   ]);\n413:   assert.equal(EMBED_WORKFLOW.mutation_boundaries.read_only, false);\n414: });\n415: \n416: test('the embed allowlist is the engine own list and nothing beside it', () => {\n417:   const boundaries = EMBED_WORKFLOW.mutation_boundaries;\n418:   const allowed = boundaries.allowed_targets.join('\\n');\n419:   for (const file of ALLOWLIST) {\n420:     assert.ok(allowed.includes(file), `${file} is missing from the workflow allowlist`);\n421:   }\n422:   const namedPaths = boundaries.allowed_targets\n423:     .map((entry) => entry.split(/[,:]/)[0].trim())\n424:     .filter((first) => first.endsWith('.md'));\n425:   assert.deepEqual([...namedPaths].sort(), [...ALLOWLIST].sort());\n426:   const forbidden = boundaries.forbidden_targets.join('\\n');\n427:   assert.match(forbidden, /agents-md-embed\\.cjs/);\n428:   assert.match(forbidden, /the git index/);\n429:   assert.match(forbidden, /\\.skilled\\/\\*\\*, which \\/doctor:update owns/);\n430: });\n431: \n432: test('the embed workflow writes only after the printed plan, its digest and the yes', () => {\n433:   const plan = phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan');\n434:   assert.match(plan, new RegExp(`${EMBED_ENGINE} plan`));\n435:   assert.doesNotMatch(plan, /--plan-digest/);\n436:   assert.match(plan, /plan-digest/);\n437: \n438:   const approval = phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_3_approval');\n439:   assert.match(approval, /Ask the embed question once/);\n440:   assert.match(approval, /the plan the operator has just read/);\n441:   assert.match(approval, /STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled/);\n442:   assert.match(approval, /naming the declined embed/);\n443:   assert.match(approval, /Nothing is written/);\n444: \n445:   const write = phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_4_write');\n446:   assert.match(write, /only after the embed yes/);\n447:   assert.match(write, /--plan-digest/);\n448:   assert.match(write, /does not match/);\n449:   assert.ok(EMBED_PHASES.indexOf('phase_3_approval') < EMBED_PHASES.indexOf('phase_4_write'));\n450:   // The write switch is the engine's own apply subcommand, and the digest is the\n451:   // plan's, so a plan approved at one tree cannot be applied at another.\n452:   assert.doesNotMatch(phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan'), /apply --plan-digest/);\n453: });\n454: \n455: test('a no at the embed question ends the run with nothing written, and a dry run ends at OK', () => {\n456:   assert.match(phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_3_approval'), /Any answer other than yes is a no/);\n457:   assert.match(phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan'), /If dry_run is true/);\n458:   assert.match(phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan'), /STATUS=OK/);\n459:   assert.match(phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan'), /asks nothing and writes nothing/);\n460:   assert.match(phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan'), /NOTHING TO DO/);\n461: });\n462: \n463: test('the embed workflow hands the undo block back instead of composing one', () => {\n464:   const report = phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_6_report');\n465:   assert.match(report, /undo block the engine printed/);\n466:   assert.match(report, /Undo:/);\n467:   assert.match(report, /Never run the undo inside this route/);\n468:   assert.match(report, /the operator commits/i);\n469: });\n470: \n471: test('the restore workflow asks once, plans from the engine, and writes only after that yes', () => {\n472:   assert.equal(RESTORE_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.execution, 'interactive');\n473:   assert.equal(RESTORE_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.approvals, 'explicit_yes');\n474:   assert.equal(RESTORE_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.never_commit, true);\n475:   assert.deepEqual(RESTORE_WORKFLOW.output.statuses, ['OK', 'CANCELLED', 'FAIL']);\n476:   assert.deepEqual(RESTORE_PHASES, [\n477:     'phase_1_read',\n478:     'phase_2_plan',\n479:     'phase_3_approval',\n480:     'phase_4_write',\n481:     'phase_5_reread',\n482:     'phase_6_report',\n483:   ]);\n484:   for (const key of routeFor('restore').setup_vars) {\n485:     assert.ok(key in RESTORE_WORKFLOW.inputs, `inputs.${key} is missing`);\n486:   }\n487:   const plan = phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan');\n488:   assert.match(plan, /restore --run=\\{run_dir\\} --dry-run/);\n489:   assert.doesNotMatch(plan, /--yes/);\n490:   const write = phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_4_write');\n491:   assert.match(write, /restore --run=\\{run_dir\\} --yes/);\n492:   assert.match(write, /only after the restore yes/);\n493:   const approval = phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_3_approval');\n494:   assert.match(approval, /STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled/);\n495:   assert.match(approval, /naming the declined restore/);\n496:   assert.match(approval, /Nothing is written/);\n497: });\n498: \n499: test('the restore workflow restores only what one run recorded, and reads the hash first', () => {\n500:   const boundaries = RESTORE_WORKFLOW.mutation_boundaries;\n501:   const allowed = boundaries.allowed_targets.join('\\n');\n502:   assert.match(allowed, /manifest\\.json/);\n503:   assert.match(allowed, /allowlist/);\n504:   const forbidden = boundaries.forbidden_targets.join('\\n');\n505:   assert.match(forbidden, /agents-md-embed\\.cjs/);\n506:   assert.match(forbidden, /the git index/);\n507:   assert.match(boundaries.invariant, /recorded hash/);\n508:   assert.match(boundaries.invariant, /STATUS=CANCELLED/);\n509:   // A restore never reads a backup directory the operator was not shown.\n510:   assert.match(phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_1_read'), /manifest\\.json/);\n511: });\n512: \n513: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n514: // 6. THE COMMAND CONTRACT, THE SETUP LIST AND THE CATALOG\n515: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n516: \n517: test('the doctor contract entry carries every field its schema requires and nothing it forbids', () => {\n518:   for (const key of FAMILY_SCHEMA.required) {\n519:     assert.ok(key in DOCTOR_CONTRACT, `families.doctor is missing ${key}`);\n520:   }\n521:   const known = new Set(Object.keys(FAMILY_SCHEMA.properties));\n522:   assert.deepEqual(\n523:     Object.keys(DOCTOR_CONTRACT).filter((key) => !known.has(key)),\n524:     [],\n525:     'the schema forbids an additional property',\n526:   );\n527:   assert.ok(FAMILY_SCHEMA.properties.topology.enum.includes(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.topology));\n528: });\n529: \n530: test('the contract names the router, the three workflows, the presentation, the hint and the alias', () => {\n531:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.router_path.includes('.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md'));\n532:   for (const asset of ['doctor-agents-md-check.yaml', 'doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml', 'doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml']) {\n533:     assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.execution_targets.some((entry) => entry.target.endsWith(asset)), asset);\n534:     assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.owned_assets.some((entry) => entry.path.endsWith(asset)), asset);\n535:   }\n536:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.owned_assets\n537:     .some((entry) => entry.purpose === 'presentation' && entry.path.endsWith('doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt')));\n538:   // A script asset carries its one-line purpose beside the path, the way the helper's\n539:   // does, so the path is matched inside the cell rather than at its end.\n540:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.owned_assets.some((entry) => entry.path.includes('agents-md-check.cjs')));\n541:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.owned_assets.some((entry) => entry.path.includes('agents-md-embed.cjs')));\n542:   const hint = ROUTER.match(/^argument-hint:\\s*\"(.*)\"$/m)[1];\n543:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.input.argument_hint.includes(`${hint} (agents-md)`));\n544:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.invocation_aliases.includes(`/doctor:agents-md ${hint}`));\n545:   const lines = DOCTOR_CONTRACT.loader_requirements.filter((line) => line.includes('/doctor:agents-md'));\n546:   const text = lines.join('\\n');\n547:   assert.match(text, /check is the read-only default target/);\n548:   assert.match(text, /plan digest/i);\n549:   assert.match(text, /restore/);\n550:   assert.match(text, /STATUS=CANCELLED/);\n551:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.destructive_policy.operations.some((line) => line.includes('agents-md embed')));\n552:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.destructive_policy.operations.some((line) => line.includes('agents-md restore')));\n553: });\n554: \n555: test('the setup target list carries one agents-md row and keeps the rest of the family', () => {\n556:   const rows = SETUP_PRESENTATION.split('\\n').filter((line) => line.includes('/doctor:agents-md'));\n557:   assert.equal(rows.length, 1);\n558:   assert.match(rows[0], /^\\| `\\/doctor:agents-md \\[check\\|embed\\|restore\\]/);\n559:   // The family's own reach check requires one row per doctor router, so a row here\n560:   // and a router file there are the same decision.\n561:   const routers = fs.readdirSync(DOCTOR)\n562:     .filter((file) => file.endsWith('.md'))\n563:     .map((file) => file.replace(/\\.md$/, ''))\n564:     .filter((name) => name !== 'helper' && !name.startsWith('local-'));\n565:   const missing = routers.filter((name) => !SETUP_PRESENTATION.includes(`/doctor:${name}`));\n566:   assert.deepEqual(missing, []);\n567: });\n568: \n569: test('the update presentation gains one line naming the check target', () => {\n570:   const lines = UPDATE_PRESENTATION.split('\\n').filter((line) => line.includes('/doctor:agents-md'));\n571:   assert.equal(lines.length, 1);\n572:   assert.match(lines[0], /\\/doctor:agents-md check$/);\n573: });\n574: \n575: test('the commands catalog lists the router and counts the folder it lives in', () => {\n576:   const rows = CATALOG.split('\\n').filter((line) => line.includes('/doctor:agents-md'));\n577:   assert.equal(rows.length, 1);\n578:   const routers = fs.readdirSync(DOCTOR).filter((file) => file.endsWith('.md') && !file.startsWith('local-'));\n579:   const groupRow = CATALOG.split('\\n').find((line) => /^\\| \\*\\*doctor\\*\\* \\|/.test(line));\n580:   assert.ok(groupRow, 'the doctor group row is missing from the catalog');\n581:   assert.equal(Number(groupRow.split('|')[3].trim()), routers.length);\n582: });\n583: \n584: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n585: // 7. REACH: THE PROBLEMS AN OPERATOR ACTUALLY WRITES\n586: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n587: \n588: const rank = (problem) => {\n589:   const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [HELPER, '--json', '--', problem], { encoding: 'utf8' });\n590:   return { status: result.status, report: JSON.parse(result.stdout) };\n591: };\n592: \n593: test('three plain-language AGENTS.md problems reach the three new routes', () => {\n594:   const cases = [\n595:     ['my agents md still has the old shipped sections and I want to know which ones are stale', '/doctor:agents-md check'],\n596:     ['embed the new shipped instructions into my agents md', '/doctor:agents-md embed'],\n597:     ['undo the agents md embed and bring back the file I had before', '/doctor:agents-md restore'],\n598:   ];\n599:   for (const [problem, runnable] of cases) {\n600:     const { status, report } = rank(problem);\n601:     assert.equal(status, 0, `${problem}: exit ${status}`);\n602:     assert.equal(report.status, 'match', problem);\n603:     assert.equal(report.candidates[0].runnable, runnable, `${problem} -> ${report.candidates[0].runnable}`);\n604:   }\n605: });\n606: \n607: test('every phrase on the three routes ranks its own route first', () => {\n608:   const { loadEntries, rankProblem } = require(HELPER);\n609:   const { entries } = loadEntries(path.resolve(DOCTOR, '..', '..', '..'));\n610:   const routable = entries.filter((entry) => entry.command !== '/doctor:helper');\n611:   const misses = [];\n612:   for (const route of ROUTES) {\n613:     const runnable = `/doctor:agents-md ${route.target}`;\n614:     assert.ok(routable.some((entry) => entry.runnable === runnable), `${runnable} has no helper entry`);\n615:     for (const phrase of route.trigger_phrases) {\n616:       const top = rankProblem(routable, phrase, {}).candidates[0];\n617:       if (!top || top.runnable !== runnable) misses.push(`\"${phrase}\" -> ${top ? top.runnable : 'no match'}`);\n618:     }\n619:   }\n620:   assert.deepEqual(misses, []);\n621: });\n622: \n623: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n624: // 8. THE LINES THE ENGINES PRINT AND THE FIELDS THAT CARRY THEM\n625: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n626: \n627: // A line an engine prints and neither the workflow keep-list nor the presentation names is\n628: // a line an agent can only drop, and a dropped pointer-sync line is a mirror reported as\n629: // verified when nothing wrote it.\n630: const embedRun = (args) => {\n631:   const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [EMBED_SCRIPT, ...args], { encoding: 'utf8', input: '' });\n632:   return { code: result.status, out: result.stdout || '', err: result.stderr || '' };\n633: };\n634: \n635: const printField = (text, name) => {\n636:   const match = new RegExp(`^${name}: (.*)$`, 'mu').exec(text);\n637:   return match === null ? null : match[1].trim();\n638: };\n639: \n640: // One composed repository per case, in a directory the case removes. Composition reads the\n641: // manifest, so a case describes the template that ships today rather than a stored copy.\n642: const composedTree = (t, name) => {\n643:   const parent = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), `doctor-agents-md-contract-${name}-`));\n644:   t.after(() => fs.rmSync(parent, { recursive: true, force: true }));\n645:   const dir = path.join(parent, name);\n646:   composeFixture(name, dir);\n647:   return dir;\n648: };\n649: \n650: // The engine never deletes a backup, so the case does: only the directory a run printed,\n651: // and only when it sits under the temporary directory it was created in.\n652: const trackBackup = (t, text) => {\n653:   for (const line of text.split('\\n')) {\n654:     const hit = /^backup: (\\S+)$/u.exec(line);\n655:     if (hit === null) continue;\n656:     const dir = hit[1];\n657:     t.after(() => {\n658:       if (!dir.startsWith(os.tmpdir() + path.sep)) return;\n659:       fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n660:     });\n661:   }\n662: };\n663: \n664: // The label of each field line an engine prints, read off its output rather than off its\n665: // source, so a line one of them gains arrives here as a failure with its own name. The\n666: // block body is skipped: its first word is the repository's, not the engine's.\n667: const printedLabels = (text) => {\n668:   const labels = new Set();\n669:   let inBlock = false;\n670:   for (const line of text.split('\\n')) {\n671:     if (line === 'block:') { inBlock = true; continue; }\n672:     if (line === 'block-end:') { inBlock = false; labels.add('block-end'); continue; }\n673:     if (inBlock) continue;\n674:     const hit = /^([a-z][a-z-]*)\\b/u.exec(line);\n675:     if (hit !== null) labels.add(hit[1]);\n676:   }\n677:   return labels;\n678: };\n679: \n680: // Where an operator meets each field line: the presentation's own field, and the phrase the\n681: // workflow keep-list uses. `note` and `finding` are pinned here too, though the fixtures\n682: // below happen not to print them, because the field has to exist for the run that does.\n683: const PRINTED_FIELDS = new Map([\n684:   ['target', { shown: /^Targets: /mu, kept: /the target list/u }],\n685:   ['note', { shown: /^Notes: /mu, kept: /each note/u }],\n686:   ['diff', { shown: /a `diff` per path/u, kept: /each diff/u }],\n687:   ['block', { shown: /^Block: /mu, kept: /`block:` and `block-end:`/u }],\n688:   ['block-end', { shown: /^Block: /mu, kept: /`block:` and `block-end:`/u }],\n689:   ['budget', { shown: /^Budget: /mu, kept: /the budget line/u }],\n690:   ['finding', { shown: /^Findings: /mu, kept: /each finding line/u }],\n691:   ['preservation', { shown: /^Preservation: /mu, kept: /the preservation line/u }],\n692:   ['backup', { shown: /^Backup folder: /mu, kept: /the backup line/u }],\n693:   ['backup-fallback', { shown: /^Backup note: /mu, kept: /the backup-fallback line/u }],\n694:   ['undo', { shown: /^Undo: /mu, kept: /the undo line/u }],\n695:   ['plan-digest', { shown: /^Plan digest: /mu, kept: /the plan-digest line/u }],\n696:   ['wrote', { shown: /^Files changed: /mu, kept: /one wrote or removed line per path/u }],\n697:   ['removed', { shown: /^Files changed: /mu, kept: /one wrote or removed line per path/u }],\n698:   ['pointer-sync', { shown: /^Pointer sync: /mu, kept: /the pointer-sync line/u }],\n699:   ['repo-rules', { shown: /^Router: /mu, kept: /the repo-rules line/u }],\n700:   ['check-after', { shown: /^Re-read: /mu, kept: /the check-after line/u }],\n701:   ['cp', { shown: /one copy line per overwritten file/u, kept: /one copy line per overwritten file/u }],\n702: ]);\n703: \n704: // The restore prints its own lines, so its plan and result templates are held to the same\n705: // rule: a folder a run created is a line an agent can only drop unless a field carries it.\n706: const RESTORE_FIELDS = new Map([\n707:   ['restore', { shown: /^Put back: /mu, kept: /one restore line per path/u }],\n708:   ['dry-run', { shown: /^Dry run: nothing was written and nothing was asked\\.$/mu, kept: /dry-run result/u }],\n709: ]);\n710: \n711: test('every field the writing engines print has a field in the presentation and a line in the keep-list', (t) => {\n712:   const dir = composedTree(t, 'claude-only');\n713:   const planned = embedRun(['plan', '--create-router', '--root', dir]);\n714:   trackBackup(t, planned.out);\n715:   assert.equal(planned.code, 0, planned.err);\n716:   const digest = printField(planned.out, 'plan-digest');\n717:   assert.match(digest || '', /^[0-9a-f]{64}$/u, 'the plan prints its digest');\n718: \n719:   const applied = embedRun(['apply', '--create-router', '--root', dir, '--plan-digest', digest]);\n720:   trackBackup(t, applied.out);\n721:   assert.equal(applied.code, 0, applied.err);\n722: \n723:   // The directory is named after the digest rather than after a clock reading, so the\n724:   // folder and the undo the operator approved are the ones apply used. A clock re-resolved\n725:   // at apply time named a directory no run ever created, and the approved undo exited 2.\n726:   assert.equal(printField(applied.out, 'backup'), printField(planned.out, 'backup'), 'apply backs up where the plan pointed');\n727:   assert.equal(printField(applied.out, 'undo'), printField(planned.out, 'undo'), 'the undo that was approved is the undo apply printed');\n728: \n729:   // The generator rewrites an existing pointer file and never creates a missing one, so a\n730:   // repository without one carries a nonzero verdict on a run that still ends STATUS=OK.\n731:   // That is the case the result template has to be able to show.\n732:   assert.match(applied.out, /^pointer-sync: exit 1 \\(.*skill-routing\\.md: missing/mu);\n733:   assert.doesNotMatch(applied.out, /wrote \\.cursor\\/rules\\/skill-routing\\.md/u);\n734: \n735:   const printed = [...printedLabels(planned.out), ...printedLabels(applied.out)];\n736:   const unnamed = [...new Set(printed)].filter((label) => !PRINTED_FIELDS.has(label)).sort();\n737:   assert.deepEqual(unnamed, [], 'an engine line no field carries');\n738: \n739:   const kept = `${phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan')}\\n${phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_4_write')}`;\n740:   for (const [label, where] of PRINTED_FIELDS) {\n741:     assert.ok(where.kept.test(kept), `${label}: the workflow keep-list does not name it`);\n742:     assert.ok(where.shown.test(PRESENTATION), `${label}: the presentation shows no field for it`);\n743:   }\n744: \n745:   // The restore templates carry the same obligation. The apply above created a .cursor\n746:   // folder for the mirror, so its plan prints the folder lines the result has to be able\n747:   // to show, and the run that removes them prints the other form of the same line.\n748:   const backup = printField(applied.out, 'backup');\n749:   const restorePlan = embedRun(['restore', `--run=${backup}`, '--root', dir, '--dry-run']);\n750:   assert.equal(restorePlan.code, 0, restorePlan.err);\n751:   assert.match(restorePlan.out, /^restore \\.cursor\\/rules\\/: remove if empty \\(this run created it\\)$/mu);\n752: \n753:   const restored = embedRun(['restore', `--run=${backup}`, '--root', dir, '--yes']);\n754:   assert.equal(restored.code, 0, restored.err);\n755:   assert.match(restored.out, /^restore \\.cursor\\/rules\\/: removed the empty folder this run created$/mu);\n756: \n757:   const restorePrinted = [...printedLabels(restorePlan.out), ...printedLabels(restored.out)];\n758:   const restoreUnnamed = [...new Set(restorePrinted)].filter((label) => !RESTORE_FIELDS.has(label)).sort();\n759:   assert.deepEqual(restoreUnnamed, [], 'a restore line no field carries');\n760: \n761:   const restoreKept = `${phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan')}\\n${phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_4_write')}`;\n762:   for (const [label, where] of RESTORE_FIELDS) {\n763:     assert.ok(where.kept.test(restoreKept), `${label}: the restore keep-list does not name it`);\n764:     assert.ok(where.shown.test(PRESENTATION), `${label}: the restore templates show no field for it`);\n765:   }\n766: \n767:   // A record names its own root, and a restore that runs against another one is refused,\n768:   // so the plan template, the result template and the route all name where that ends.\n769:   const refused = embedRun(['restore', `--run=${backup}`, '--yes']);\n770:   assert.equal(refused.code, 2, 'a restore against another root exits 2');\n771:   assert.match(refused.err, /ERROR: the record names the root .*pass --root/u);\n772:   const restorePlanTemplate = PRESENTATION.split('## 5. Restore Plan and Approval')[1].split(/\\n## 6\\./u)[0];\n773:   const restoredTemplate = PRESENTATION.split('### Restored')[1].split('### Failure Summary')[0];\n774:   assert.match(restorePlanTemplate, /^Folders: /mu, 'the plan template has no field for the folder lines');\n775:   assert.match(restoredTemplate, /^Folders: /mu, 'the result template has no field for the folder lines');\n776:   assert.match(restorePlanTemplate, /names another root/u);\n777:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| A restore reports that the record names another root \\|/mu);\n778:   assert.match(phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan'), /names a root other than the one this restore runs against/u);\n779:   assert.match(phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_4_write'), /names another root/u);\n780: });\n781: \n782: test('a plan on a repository with no router names the absent target and the backup note', (t) => {\n783:   const dir = composedTree(t, 'foreign');\n784:   const planned = embedRun(['plan', '--root', dir]);\n785:   assert.equal(planned.code, 0, planned.err);\n786: \n787:   // Two lines a plan prints that no field carried: the fifth target action, and the note\n788:   // that explains a backup placed outside the repository.\n789:   assert.match(planned.out, /^target REPO RULES\\.md: absent$/mu);\n790:   assert.match(planned.out, /^note: /mu);\n791:   assert.match(planned.out, /^backup-fallback: /mu);\n792: \n793:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /<create\\|replace\\|remove\\|unchanged\\|absent>/u);\n794:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /`absent` means the path is not there/u);\n795:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^Backup note: /mu);\n796:   const plan = phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan');\n797:   assert.match(plan, /absent/u);\n798:   assert.match(plan, /backup-fallback/u);\n799: });\n800: \n801: test('an embed whose pointer sync did not verify names the mirror it could not write', () => {\n802:   const embedded = PRESENTATION.split('### Embedded')[1].split('### Unchanged')[0];\n803:   for (const name of ['Pointer sync:', 'Router:', 'Next:']) {\n804:     assert.match(embedded, new RegExp(`^${name} `, 'mu'), `${name} is not a field of the result`);\n805:   }\n806: \n807:   const write = phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_4_write');\n808:   assert.match(write, /nonzero/u);\n809:   assert.match(write, /Next:.*\\/doctor:runtime-mirrors/u, 'a nonzero pointer sync names the mirror route as the next step');\n810:   assert.match(write, /never creates/u, 'the generator cannot create a missing pointer file');\n811:   assert.match(write, /Files changed/u, 'the file it cannot create is never listed as written');\n812: \n813:   // A repair for the row the re-read still reports, and a next step for the line that says\n814:   // why: the check route can only report that row again.\n815:   const troubleshooting = PRESENTATION.split('## 7. Troubleshooting Display')[1].split(/\\n## 8\\./u)[0];\n816:   const row = troubleshooting.split('\\n').find((line) => /^\\| `A10`/u.test(line));\n817:   assert.ok(row, 'the troubleshooting table has no A10 row');\n818:   assert.match(row, /\\/doctor:runtime-mirrors/u);\n819: \n820:   const nextRow = PRESENTATION.split('## 8. Next Step')[1].split('\\n').find((line) => /pointer-sync/u.test(line));\n821:   assert.ok(nextRow, 'the next-step table has no pointer-sync row');\n822:   assert.match(nextRow, /\\/doctor:runtime-mirrors/u);\n823: });","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs, lines 1-823\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3: // MODULE: Doctor Agents-MD Contract Tests\n4: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: // Holds /doctor:agents-md together: the three routes in the manifest, the router,\n8: // the presentation contract, the three workflows and the command contract must\n9: // agree on the targets, the mutation classes, the asset paths, the engines they\n10: // name and the order a write happens in.\n11: //\n12: // The route validator checks structure and the engines' own suites check the bytes\n13: // they produce. What nothing else can see is the promise between the two: that the\n14: // writing workflow is shaped as plan, digest, yes and only then a write, that a no\n15: // leaves the tree exactly as it was, that the workflow's allowlist is the engine's\n16: // own list rather than a second one that drifts from it, and that the router stays\n17: // a router. This suite asserts those promises by reading the files.\n18: \n19: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n20: // 1. IMPORTS AND FIXTURES\n21: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n22: \n23: const assert = require('node:assert/strict');\n24: const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n25: const fs = require('node:fs');\n26: const os = require('node:os');\n27: const path = require('node:path');\n28: const test = require('node:test');\n29: const { parse: parseYaml } = require('yaml');\n30: \n31: const { composeFixture } = require('./fixtures/agents-md/compose-fixture.cjs');\n32: \n33: const DOCTOR = path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..');\n34: const ASSETS = path.join(DOCTOR, 'assets');\n35: const SCRIPTS = path.join(DOCTOR, 'scripts');\n36: const COMMANDS = path.resolve(DOCTOR, '..');\n37: const SKILL_DOC_ASSETS = path.resolve(DOCTOR, '..', '..', 'skills', 'sk-doc', 'sk-create-command', 'assets');\n38: \n39: const read = (file) => fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n40: \n41: const MANIFEST = parseYaml(read(path.join(DOCTOR, '_routes.yaml')));\n42: const ROUTES = MANIFEST.routes.filter((route) => route.command === '/doctor:agents-md');\n43: const routeFor = (target) => ROUTES.find((route) => route.target === target);\n44: \n45: const ROUTER = read(path.join(DOCTOR, 'agents-md.md'));\n46: const PRESENTATION = read(path.join(ASSETS, 'doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt'));\n47: const CHECK_YAML = read(path.join(ASSETS, 'doctor-agents-md-check.yaml'));\n48: const EMBED_YAML = read(path.join(ASSETS, 'doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml'));\n49: const RESTORE_YAML = read(path.join(ASSETS, 'doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml'));\n50: const SETUP_PRESENTATION = read(path.join(ASSETS, 'doctor-setup-presentation.txt'));\n51: const UPDATE_PRESENTATION = read(path.join(ASSETS, 'doctor-update-presentation.txt'));\n52: const CATALOG = read(path.join(COMMANDS, 'README.txt'));\n53: \n54: const CONTRACT = JSON.parse(read(path.join(SKILL_DOC_ASSETS, 'command-contract.json')));\n55: const SCHEMA = JSON.parse(read(path.join(SKILL_DOC_ASSETS, 'command-contract.schema.json')));\n56: const DOCTOR_CONTRACT = CONTRACT.families.doctor;\n57: const FAMILY_SCHEMA = SCHEMA.definitions.familyContract;\n58: \n59: const CHECK_ENGINE = '.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs';\n60: const EMBED_ENGINE = '.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs';\n61: const HELPER = path.join(SCRIPTS, 'doctor-helper-match.cjs');\n62: const EMBED_SCRIPT = path.join(SCRIPTS, 'agents-md-embed.cjs');\n63: \n64: // The engine's own write boundary, read from the engine. A second copy in the\n65: // workflow is the drift this suite exists to catch, so the allowlist cases compare\n66: // against this list rather than against a literal here.\n67: const { ALLOWLIST } = require(path.join(SCRIPTS, 'agents-md-embed.cjs'));\n68: \n69: const engineOf = (entry) => entry.match(/\\.skilled\\/\\S+\\.cjs/)[0];\n70: \n71: const CHECK_WORKFLOW = parseYaml(CHECK_YAML);\n72: const EMBED_WORKFLOW = parseYaml(EMBED_YAML);\n73: const RESTORE_WORKFLOW = parseYaml(RESTORE_YAML);\n74: const EMBED_PHASES = Object.keys(EMBED_WORKFLOW.workflow);\n75: const RESTORE_PHASES = Object.keys(RESTORE_WORKFLOW.workflow);\n76: \n77: const yamlStrings = (node, out = []) => {\n78:   if (Array.isArray(node)) {\n79:     for (const value of node) yamlStrings(value, out);\n80:   } else if (node && typeof node === 'object') {\n81:     for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(node)) {\n82:       out.push(key);\n83:       yamlStrings(value, out);\n84:     }\n85:   } else if (typeof node === 'string') {\n86:     out.push(node);\n87:   }\n88:   return out;\n89: };\n90: \n91: const phaseText = (workflow, phase) => yamlStrings(workflow.workflow[phase]).join('\\n');\n92: \n93: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n94: // 2. THE ROUTES\n95: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n96: \n97: test('the manifest holds a check, an embed and a restore route, and only check answers the bare command', () => {\n98:   assert.deepEqual(ROUTES.map((route) => route.target), ['check', 'embed', 'restore']);\n99:   // Three targets make the command multi-target, so the read-only one has to claim\n100:   // the bare invocation: without the flag a typed /doctor:agents-md would reach no\n101:   // bridge at all, and a bare invocation must never reach a route that writes.\n102:   assert.equal(routeFor('check').default_target, true);\n103:   assert.equal(routeFor('embed').default_target, undefined);\n104:   assert.equal(routeFor('restore').default_target, undefined);\n105:   assert.equal(routeFor('check').mutating, 'read-only');\n106:   assert.match(routeFor('check').gate3_location, /^n\\/a/);\n107:   assert.equal(routeFor('embed').mutating, 'mutates');\n108:   assert.equal(routeFor('restore').mutating, 'mutates');\n109:   for (const route of ROUTES) {\n110:     assert.equal(route.yaml, `doctor-agents-md-${route.target}.yaml`);\n111:     assert.ok(fs.existsSync(path.join(ASSETS, route.yaml)), route.yaml);\n112:     assert.deepEqual(route.mcp_tools, []);\n113:   }\n114:   assert.deepEqual(routeFor('check').allowed_flags, ['--json', '--root <dir>']);\n115:   assert.deepEqual([...routeFor('embed').allowed_flags].sort(), [\n116:     '--create-router',\n117:     '--dry-run',\n118:     '--keep-claude-md',\n119:     '--plan-digest <digest>',\n120:     '--remove-claude-md',\n121:     '--root <dir>',\n122:   ].sort());\n123:   assert.deepEqual([...routeFor('restore').allowed_flags].sort(), ['--dry-run', '--run <dir>', '--yes'].sort());\n124: });\n125: \n126: // The header is the file's own table of contents, and a reader who trusts it misses every\n127: // router it omits. The count is the folder's, so a new router file fails here until the\n128: // header names it.\n129: test('the route manifest header lists every router file in the folder', () => {\n130:   const header = read(path.join(DOCTOR, '_routes.yaml')).split(/^schema_version:/m)[0];\n131:   const listed = [...header.matchAll(/^#   \\/doctor:(\\S+)\\s+\\S+\\.md$/gm)].map((match) => match[1]).sort();\n132:   const routers = fs.readdirSync(DOCTOR)\n133:     .filter((file) => file.endsWith('.md') && !file.startsWith('local-'))\n134:     .map((file) => file.replace(/\\.md$/, ''))\n135:     .sort();\n136:   assert.deepEqual(listed, routers, 'the header names every router or the count in it is wrong');\n137: });\n138: \n139: test('the writing routes name every place the engines write and nothing else', () => {\n140:   const embed = routeFor('embed').gate3_location;\n141:   // Exactly the six allowlisted paths, the backup that makes the write reversible and\n142:   // the digest that decides whether the approved bytes are the bytes on disk.\n143:   for (const expected of [\n144:     /AGENTS\\.md/,\n145:     /CLAUDE\\.md/,\n146:     /\\.codex\\/AGENTS\\.md/,\n147:     /\\.cursor\\/rules\\/repo-local\\.md/,\n148:     /\\.cursor\\/rules\\/skill-routing\\.md/,\n149:     /REPO RULES\\.md/,\n150:     /backup/i,\n151:     /plan digest/i,\n152:   ]) {\n153:     assert.match(embed, expected);\n154:   }\n155:   // A release unit belongs to /doctor:update, and no embed run stages a commit.\n156:   assert.doesNotMatch(embed, /\\.skilled\\/skills|the git index|commit/i);\n157: \n158:   const restore = routeFor('restore').gate3_location;\n159:   assert.match(restore, /manifest\\.json/);\n160:   assert.match(restore, /allowlist/);\n161:   assert.match(restore, /recorded/);\n162: });\n163: \n164: test('every route names the engine calls its workflow runs and every trigger phrase carries three or more words', () => {\n165:   for (const route of ROUTES) {\n166:     for (const phrase of route.trigger_phrases) {\n167:       assert.ok(phrase.trim().split(/\\s+/).length >= 3, phrase);\n168:     }\n169:   }\n170:   // The check route reads, and only reads.\n171:   assert.deepEqual(routeFor('check').script_invocations.map(engineOf), [CHECK_ENGINE]);\n172: \n173:   // The plan writes nothing, the apply carries the digest the plan printed, and the\n174:   // re-read proves what landed. A plan call that already carried the digest would\n175:   // make the approval a formality, so it never does.\n176:   const embedCalls = routeFor('embed').script_invocations;\n177:   assert.deepEqual(embedCalls.map(engineOf), [EMBED_ENGINE, EMBED_ENGINE, CHECK_ENGINE]);\n178:   assert.match(embedCalls[0], /agents-md-embed\\.cjs plan/);\n179:   assert.doesNotMatch(embedCalls[0], /--plan-digest/);\n180:   assert.match(embedCalls[1], /agents-md-embed\\.cjs apply/);\n181:   assert.match(embedCalls[1], /--plan-digest <digest>/);\n182: \n183:   // The restore plan is the engine's own dry run, and the write repeats the record\n184:   // path the operator was shown.\n185:   const restoreCalls = routeFor('restore').script_invocations;\n186:   assert.deepEqual(restoreCalls.map(engineOf), [EMBED_ENGINE, EMBED_ENGINE, CHECK_ENGINE]);\n187:   assert.match(restoreCalls[0], /agents-md-embed\\.cjs restore --run=<dir> --dry-run/);\n188:   assert.match(restoreCalls[1], /agents-md-embed\\.cjs restore --run=<dir> --yes/);\n189:   assert.doesNotMatch(restoreCalls[0], /--yes/);\n190: });\n191: \n192: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n193: // 3. ROUTER AND PRESENTATION\n194: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n195: \n196: test('the router follows the router template: six canonical sections in order and no inline presentation', () => {\n197:   const headings = [...ROUTER.matchAll(/^## \\d+\\. ([A-Z ]+)$/gm)].map((match) => match[1]);\n198:   assert.deepEqual(headings, [\n199:     'ROUTER CONTRACT',\n200:     'OWNED ASSETS',\n201:     'MODE ROUTING',\n202:     'EXECUTION TARGETS',\n203:     'PRESENTATION BOUNDARY',\n204:     'WORKFLOW SUMMARY',\n205:   ]);\n206:   // A fenced block or a status line in the router would put a dashboard or a result\n207:   // template inline, where the presentation contract is the only place they belong.\n208:   assert.doesNotMatch(ROUTER, /```/);\n209:   assert.doesNotMatch(ROUTER, /STATUS=/);\n210: });\n211: \n212: test('the router frontmatter stays within budget and grants only the tools it uses', () => {\n213:   const description = ROUTER.match(/^description:\\s*\"(.*)\"$/m)[1];\n214:   assert.ok(description.length <= 110, `description is ${description.length} chars`);\n215:   assert.doesNotMatch(description, /[<>]/);\n216:   const hint = ROUTER.match(/^argument-hint:\\s*\"(.*)\"$/m)[1];\n217:   assert.ok(hint.length <= 140, `argument-hint is ${hint.length} chars`);\n218:   for (const token of ['[check|embed|restore]', '[--json]', '[--root <dir>]', '[--dry-run]', '[--plan-digest <digest>]', '[--run <dir>]', '[--yes]']) {\n219:     assert.ok(hint.includes(token), token);\n220:   }\n221:   const tools = ROUTER.match(/^allowed-tools:\\s*(.+)$/m)[1].split(',').map((tool) => tool.trim());\n222:   assert.deepEqual(tools, ['Read', 'Bash']);\n223:   // Instruction-document authoring is sk-doc's, so that is the one skill tag here.\n224:   assert.equal(ROUTER.split('<!-- skill_agent: system-skilled-doctor -->').length - 1, 1);\n225: });\n226: \n227: test('the router binds each target to the workflow asset its route names', () => {\n228:   for (const route of ROUTES) {\n229:     assert.match(\n230:       ROUTER,\n231:       new RegExp(`^\\\\| \\`${route.target}\\` \\\\| \\`\\\\.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/${route.yaml}\\` \\\\|$`, 'm'),\n232:       route.target,\n233:     );\n234:   }\n235: });\n236: \n237: test('the router names both engines as owned assets and composes nothing itself', () => {\n238:   const owned = ROUTER.split('## 2. OWNED ASSETS')[1].split('## 3.')[0];\n239:   assert.ok(owned.includes(CHECK_ENGINE), CHECK_ENGINE);\n240:   assert.ok(owned.includes(EMBED_ENGINE), EMBED_ENGINE);\n241:   assert.match(ROUTER, /Do not compose an `AGENTS\\.md` byte/);\n242: });\n243: \n244: test('the router resolves the bare command to check and keeps every write behind the digest and a yes', () => {\n245:   assert.match(ROUTER, /`default_target`/);\n246:   assert.match(ROUTER, /A bare `\\/doctor:agents-md` never reaches `embed` or `restore`, which write/);\n247:   assert.match(ROUTER, /never runs `apply` without the digest its own plan printed/);\n248:   assert.match(ROUTER, /never runs a writing target without its yes/);\n249: });\n250: \n251: test('the router step list runs the real order: plan, digest, yes, apply, re-read', () => {\n252:   const summary = ROUTER.split('## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY')[1];\n253:   const steps = summary.split('\\n').map((line) => line.trim()).filter((line) => /^\\d+\\. /.test(line));\n254:   const at = (pattern) => {\n255:     const index = steps.findIndex((step) => pattern.test(step));\n256:     assert.ok(index >= 0, `no step names ${pattern}`);\n257:     return index;\n258:   };\n259:   const plan = at(/agents-md-embed\\.cjs plan/);\n260:   const digest = at(/the plan digest/);\n261:   const question = at(/asks the embed question/);\n262:   const apply = at(/agents-md-embed\\.cjs apply --plan-digest/);\n263:   const reread = at(/re-reads the written repository/);\n264:   assert.ok(plan < digest, 'the plan is printed before its digest is offered');\n265:   assert.ok(digest < question, 'the digest is named before the question');\n266:   assert.ok(question < apply, 'the apply runs only after the question');\n267:   assert.ok(apply < reread, 'the re-read follows the write');\n268:   const stepText = steps.join('\\n');\n269:   assert.match(stepText, /ends the run as cancelled/);\n270:   assert.match(stepText, /nothing is written/);\n271:   assert.match(stepText, /restore/);\n272: });\n273: \n274: test('the presentation carries the menu, the accepted answers, the manifest rows and the valid targets line', () => {\n275:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^## 1\\. Argument Failure$/m);\n276:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^1\\) check$/m);\n277:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^2\\) embed$/m);\n278:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^3\\) restore$/m);\n279:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| `1` \\| target = `check` \\|/m);\n280:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| `2` \\| target = `embed` \\|/m);\n281:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| `3` \\| target = `restore` \\|/m);\n282:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^Valid targets: check, embed, restore$/m);\n283:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| `check` \\| `doctor-agents-md-check\\.yaml` \\| read-only \\|/m);\n284:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| `embed` \\| `doctor-agents-md-embed\\.yaml` \\| mutates \\|/m);\n285:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| `restore` \\| `doctor-agents-md-restore\\.yaml` \\| mutates \\|/m);\n286: });\n287: \n288: // A failure the router promises to catch has to have wording, or the agent invents one and\n289: // the operand hears a sentence the contract never approved. A value flag at the end of the\n290: // line and a second positional are the two an operator reaches by hand.\n291: test('the argument table defines a missing value and a second positional for every target', () => {\n292:   const table = PRESENTATION.split('## 1. Argument Failure')[1].split(/\\n## 2\\./u)[0];\n293:   const rows = table.split('\\n').filter((line) => line.startsWith('| '));\n294: \n295:   const missing = rows.find((line) => /value flag/u.test(line));\n296:   assert.ok(missing, 'no row for a value flag given without its value');\n297:   for (const flag of ['--plan-digest', '--root']) assert.ok(missing.includes(flag), `${flag} is not named`);\n298:   assert.match(missing, /STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"missing_argument\"/u);\n299:   assert.match(missing, /Try: /u);\n300: \n301:   const second = rows.find((line) => /second positional/u.test(line));\n302:   assert.ok(second, 'no row for a second positional');\n303:   // One suggestion per target, because the right next command differs by target.\n304:   assert.match(second, /\\/doctor:agents-md check \\[--json\\] \\[--root <dir>\\]/u);\n305:   assert.match(second, /\\/doctor:agents-md embed \\[--dry-run\\]/u);\n306:   assert.match(second, /\\/doctor:agents-md restore --run=<dir>/u);\n307:   assert.match(second, /STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"too_many_arguments\"/u);\n308: \n309:   // The router promises this table covers both cases, so it has to name them.\n310:   assert.match(ROUTER, /a value flag without its value/u);\n311:   assert.match(ROUTER, /a second positional/u);\n312: });\n313: \n314: // The engine has three outcomes for an exit 1 and the route has to mirror all three: a row\n315: // that could not be answered is not a finding, and reporting it as one sends the operator\n316: // looking for a fault that was never found.\n317: test('an unproven row ends the check as UNKNOWN, never as a finding', () => {\n318:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^Status: \\[OK\\|FINDINGS\\|UNKNOWN\\|ERROR\\]$/mu);\n319:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^STATUS=\\[OK\\|FINDINGS\\|UNKNOWN\\]$/mu);\n320:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /exit 1 with `findings=0` ends `STATUS=UNKNOWN`/u);\n321:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /never `STATUS=FINDINGS`/u);\n322:   const { output } = CHECK_WORKFLOW;\n323:   assert.match(output, /STATUS=UNKNOWN/u);\n324:   assert.match(output, /findings=0/u);\n325: });\n326: \n327: test('the presentation keeps the check table, the JSON passthrough and the digest it makes the operator approve', () => {\n328:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^Agents instruction check: \\[the root the engine read\\]$/m);\n329:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^DOCTOR TARGET UNCHANGED$/m);\n330:   assert.ok(PRESENTATION.includes(\"With `--json` print the engine's JSON and nothing else\"));\n331:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^Plan digest: \\[the engine's plan-digest line\\]$/m);\n332:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /Embed these files now\\? \\[yes\\/no\\]$/m);\n333:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /Restore these paths from that backup now\\? \\[yes\\/no\\]$/m);\n334:   // The digest is what the operator approves, so the wording has to say so.\n335:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /the digest on screen is the digest the apply repeats/);\n336:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /never compose a plan digest/);\n337: });\n338: \n339: test('the presentation closes on the unchanged, cancelled, dry-run, restored and failed templates', () => {\n340:   // Every status a route can print appears as its own line, because a workflow that\n341:   // ends on one of them must have been told the exact string.\n342:   for (const status of ['STATUS=OK', 'STATUS=FINDINGS', 'STATUS=UNKNOWN', 'STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled', 'STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"', 'STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"']) {\n343:     assert.match(PRESENTATION, new RegExp(`^${status.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, '\\\\$&')}$`, 'm'), status);\n344:   }\n345:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled$/m);\n346:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"\\[code\\]\"$/m);\n347:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"\\[message\\]\"$/m);\n348:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /Declined: \\[the embed \\| the restore\\]/);\n349:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next\\?`$/m);\n350: });\n351: \n352: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n353: // 4. THE CHECK WORKFLOW\n354: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n355: \n356: test('the check workflow is read-only and runs the check engine the route declares', () => {\n357:   assert.equal(CHECK_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.execution, 'read_only');\n358:   assert.equal(CHECK_WORKFLOW.mutation_boundaries.read_only, true);\n359:   assert.deepEqual(CHECK_WORKFLOW.mutation_boundaries.allowed_targets, []);\n360:   assert.ok(CHECK_YAML.includes(CHECK_ENGINE), CHECK_ENGINE);\n361: });\n362: \n363: test('the check workflow declares every variable its route resolves', () => {\n364:   for (const key of routeFor('check').setup_vars) {\n365:     assert.ok(key in CHECK_WORKFLOW.inputs, `inputs.${key} is missing`);\n366:   }\n367: });\n368: \n369: test('the check workflow passes --json and --root only when the operator asked', () => {\n370:   assert.match(CHECK_WORKFLOW.inputs.json_output, /true when --json is passed/);\n371:   assert.match(CHECK_YAML, /--json when the operator/);\n372:   assert.doesNotMatch(CHECK_YAML, /agents-md-check\\.cjs --json/);\n373:   assert.match(CHECK_WORKFLOW.inputs.root, /--root <dir>/);\n374:   // The default root is the repository the operator is in, so an unconditional\n375:   // --root would classify somebody else's tree.\n376:   assert.doesNotMatch(CHECK_YAML, /agents-md-check\\.cjs --root/);\n377: });\n378: \n379: test('the check workflow maps the engine exit classes to a route status', () => {\n380:   const { output } = CHECK_WORKFLOW;\n381:   assert.match(output, /STATUS=OK/);\n382:   assert.match(output, /STATUS=FINDINGS/);\n383:   // Exit 1 covers two outcomes, and the route has to keep them apart: a row nobody could\n384:   // answer is not a finding, and calling it one sends the operator after a fault that was\n385:   // never found.\n386:   assert.match(output, /STATUS=UNKNOWN/);\n387:   assert.match(output, /findings=0/);\n388:   assert.match(output, /STATUS=ERROR/);\n389: });\n390: \n391: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n392: // 5. THE EMBED AND RESTORE WORKFLOWS\n393: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n394: \n395: test('the embed workflow is interactive, writes only on a yes and never commits', () => {\n396:   assert.equal(EMBED_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.execution, 'interactive');\n397:   assert.equal(EMBED_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.approvals, 'explicit_yes');\n398:   assert.equal(EMBED_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.dry_run, 'print_the_plan_then_status_ok_without_asking');\n399:   assert.equal(EMBED_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.never_commit, true);\n400:   assert.deepEqual(EMBED_WORKFLOW.output.statuses, ['OK', 'CANCELLED', 'FAIL']);\n401:   assert.equal(EMBED_WORKFLOW.output.presentation, '.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt');\n402: });\n403: \n404: test('the embed workflow runs its phases in the read, plan, approval, write, re-read, report order', () => {\n405:   assert.deepEqual(EMBED_PHASES, [\n406:     'phase_1_read',\n407:     'phase_2_plan',\n408:     'phase_3_approval',\n409:     'phase_4_write',\n410:     'phase_5_reread',\n411:     'phase_6_report',\n412:   ]);\n413:   assert.equal(EMBED_WORKFLOW.mutation_boundaries.read_only, false);\n414: });\n415: \n416: test('the embed allowlist is the engine own list and nothing beside it', () => {\n417:   const boundaries = EMBED_WORKFLOW.mutation_boundaries;\n418:   const allowed = boundaries.allowed_targets.join('\\n');\n419:   for (const file of ALLOWLIST) {\n420:     assert.ok(allowed.includes(file), `${file} is missing from the workflow allowlist`);\n421:   }\n422:   const namedPaths = boundaries.allowed_targets\n423:     .map((entry) => entry.split(/[,:]/)[0].trim())\n424:     .filter((first) => first.endsWith('.md'));\n425:   assert.deepEqual([...namedPaths].sort(), [...ALLOWLIST].sort());\n426:   const forbidden = boundaries.forbidden_targets.join('\\n');\n427:   assert.match(forbidden, /agents-md-embed\\.cjs/);\n428:   assert.match(forbidden, /the git index/);\n429:   assert.match(forbidden, /\\.skilled\\/\\*\\*, which \\/doctor:update owns/);\n430: });\n431: \n432: test('the embed workflow writes only after the printed plan, its digest and the yes', () => {\n433:   const plan = phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan');\n434:   assert.match(plan, new RegExp(`${EMBED_ENGINE} plan`));\n435:   assert.doesNotMatch(plan, /--plan-digest/);\n436:   assert.match(plan, /plan-digest/);\n437: \n438:   const approval = phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_3_approval');\n439:   assert.match(approval, /Ask the embed question once/);\n440:   assert.match(approval, /the plan the operator has just read/);\n441:   assert.match(approval, /STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled/);\n442:   assert.match(approval, /naming the declined embed/);\n443:   assert.match(approval, /Nothing is written/);\n444: \n445:   const write = phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_4_write');\n446:   assert.match(write, /only after the embed yes/);\n447:   assert.match(write, /--plan-digest/);\n448:   assert.match(write, /does not match/);\n449:   assert.ok(EMBED_PHASES.indexOf('phase_3_approval') < EMBED_PHASES.indexOf('phase_4_write'));\n450:   // The write switch is the engine's own apply subcommand, and the digest is the\n451:   // plan's, so a plan approved at one tree cannot be applied at another.\n452:   assert.doesNotMatch(phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan'), /apply --plan-digest/);\n453: });\n454: \n455: test('a no at the embed question ends the run with nothing written, and a dry run ends at OK', () => {\n456:   assert.match(phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_3_approval'), /Any answer other than yes is a no/);\n457:   assert.match(phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan'), /If dry_run is true/);\n458:   assert.match(phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan'), /STATUS=OK/);\n459:   assert.match(phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan'), /asks nothing and writes nothing/);\n460:   assert.match(phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan'), /NOTHING TO DO/);\n461: });\n462: \n463: test('the embed workflow hands the undo block back instead of composing one', () => {\n464:   const report = phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_6_report');\n465:   assert.match(report, /undo block the engine printed/);\n466:   assert.match(report, /Undo:/);\n467:   assert.match(report, /Never run the undo inside this route/);\n468:   assert.match(report, /the operator commits/i);\n469: });\n470: \n471: test('the restore workflow asks once, plans from the engine, and writes only after that yes', () => {\n472:   assert.equal(RESTORE_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.execution, 'interactive');\n473:   assert.equal(RESTORE_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.approvals, 'explicit_yes');\n474:   assert.equal(RESTORE_WORKFLOW.operating_mode.never_commit, true);\n475:   assert.deepEqual(RESTORE_WORKFLOW.output.statuses, ['OK', 'CANCELLED', 'FAIL']);\n476:   assert.deepEqual(RESTORE_PHASES, [\n477:     'phase_1_read',\n478:     'phase_2_plan',\n479:     'phase_3_approval',\n480:     'phase_4_write',\n481:     'phase_5_reread',\n482:     'phase_6_report',\n483:   ]);\n484:   for (const key of routeFor('restore').setup_vars) {\n485:     assert.ok(key in RESTORE_WORKFLOW.inputs, `inputs.${key} is missing`);\n486:   }\n487:   const plan = phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan');\n488:   assert.match(plan, /restore --run=\\{run_dir\\} --dry-run/);\n489:   assert.doesNotMatch(plan, /--yes/);\n490:   const write = phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_4_write');\n491:   assert.match(write, /restore --run=\\{run_dir\\} --yes/);\n492:   assert.match(write, /only after the restore yes/);\n493:   const approval = phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_3_approval');\n494:   assert.match(approval, /STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled/);\n495:   assert.match(approval, /naming the declined restore/);\n496:   assert.match(approval, /Nothing is written/);\n497: });\n498: \n499: test('the restore workflow restores only what one run recorded, and reads the hash first', () => {\n500:   const boundaries = RESTORE_WORKFLOW.mutation_boundaries;\n501:   const allowed = boundaries.allowed_targets.join('\\n');\n502:   assert.match(allowed, /manifest\\.json/);\n503:   assert.match(allowed, /allowlist/);\n504:   const forbidden = boundaries.forbidden_targets.join('\\n');\n505:   assert.match(forbidden, /agents-md-embed\\.cjs/);\n506:   assert.match(forbidden, /the git index/);\n507:   assert.match(boundaries.invariant, /recorded hash/);\n508:   assert.match(boundaries.invariant, /STATUS=CANCELLED/);\n509:   // A restore never reads a backup directory the operator was not shown.\n510:   assert.match(phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_1_read'), /manifest\\.json/);\n511: });\n512: \n513: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n514: // 6. THE COMMAND CONTRACT, THE SETUP LIST AND THE CATALOG\n515: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n516: \n517: test('the doctor contract entry carries every field its schema requires and nothing it forbids', () => {\n518:   for (const key of FAMILY_SCHEMA.required) {\n519:     assert.ok(key in DOCTOR_CONTRACT, `families.doctor is missing ${key}`);\n520:   }\n521:   const known = new Set(Object.keys(FAMILY_SCHEMA.properties));\n522:   assert.deepEqual(\n523:     Object.keys(DOCTOR_CONTRACT).filter((key) => !known.has(key)),\n524:     [],\n525:     'the schema forbids an additional property',\n526:   );\n527:   assert.ok(FAMILY_SCHEMA.properties.topology.enum.includes(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.topology));\n528: });\n529: \n530: test('the contract names the router, the three workflows, the presentation, the hint and the alias', () => {\n531:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.router_path.includes('.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md'));\n532:   for (const asset of ['doctor-agents-md-check.yaml', 'doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml', 'doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml']) {\n533:     assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.execution_targets.some((entry) => entry.target.endsWith(asset)), asset);\n534:     assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.owned_assets.some((entry) => entry.path.endsWith(asset)), asset);\n535:   }\n536:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.owned_assets\n537:     .some((entry) => entry.purpose === 'presentation' && entry.path.endsWith('doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt')));\n538:   // A script asset carries its one-line purpose beside the path, the way the helper's\n539:   // does, so the path is matched inside the cell rather than at its end.\n540:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.owned_assets.some((entry) => entry.path.includes('agents-md-check.cjs')));\n541:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.owned_assets.some((entry) => entry.path.includes('agents-md-embed.cjs')));\n542:   const hint = ROUTER.match(/^argument-hint:\\s*\"(.*)\"$/m)[1];\n543:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.input.argument_hint.includes(`${hint} (agents-md)`));\n544:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.invocation_aliases.includes(`/doctor:agents-md ${hint}`));\n545:   const lines = DOCTOR_CONTRACT.loader_requirements.filter((line) => line.includes('/doctor:agents-md'));\n546:   const text = lines.join('\\n');\n547:   assert.match(text, /check is the read-only default target/);\n548:   assert.match(text, /plan digest/i);\n549:   assert.match(text, /restore/);\n550:   assert.match(text, /STATUS=CANCELLED/);\n551:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.destructive_policy.operations.some((line) => line.includes('agents-md embed')));\n552:   assert.ok(DOCTOR_CONTRACT.destructive_policy.operations.some((line) => line.includes('agents-md restore')));\n553: });\n554: \n555: test('the setup target list carries one agents-md row and keeps the rest of the family', () => {\n556:   const rows = SETUP_PRESENTATION.split('\\n').filter((line) => line.includes('/doctor:agents-md'));\n557:   assert.equal(rows.length, 1);\n558:   assert.match(rows[0], /^\\| `\\/doctor:agents-md \\[check\\|embed\\|restore\\]/);\n559:   // The family's own reach check requires one row per doctor router, so a row here\n560:   // and a router file there are the same decision.\n561:   const routers = fs.readdirSync(DOCTOR)\n562:     .filter((file) => file.endsWith('.md'))\n563:     .map((file) => file.replace(/\\.md$/, ''))\n564:     .filter((name) => name !== 'helper' && !name.startsWith('local-'));\n565:   const missing = routers.filter((name) => !SETUP_PRESENTATION.includes(`/doctor:${name}`));\n566:   assert.deepEqual(missing, []);\n567: });\n568: \n569: test('the update presentation gains one line naming the check target', () => {\n570:   const lines = UPDATE_PRESENTATION.split('\\n').filter((line) => line.includes('/doctor:agents-md'));\n571:   assert.equal(lines.length, 1);\n572:   assert.match(lines[0], /\\/doctor:agents-md check$/);\n573: });\n574: \n575: test('the commands catalog lists the router and counts the folder it lives in', () => {\n576:   const rows = CATALOG.split('\\n').filter((line) => line.includes('/doctor:agents-md'));\n577:   assert.equal(rows.length, 1);\n578:   const routers = fs.readdirSync(DOCTOR).filter((file) => file.endsWith('.md') && !file.startsWith('local-'));\n579:   const groupRow = CATALOG.split('\\n').find((line) => /^\\| \\*\\*doctor\\*\\* \\|/.test(line));\n580:   assert.ok(groupRow, 'the doctor group row is missing from the catalog');\n581:   assert.equal(Number(groupRow.split('|')[3].trim()), routers.length);\n582: });\n583: \n584: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n585: // 7. REACH: THE PROBLEMS AN OPERATOR ACTUALLY WRITES\n586: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n587: \n588: const rank = (problem) => {\n589:   const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [HELPER, '--json', '--', problem], { encoding: 'utf8' });\n590:   return { status: result.status, report: JSON.parse(result.stdout) };\n591: };\n592: \n593: test('three plain-language AGENTS.md problems reach the three new routes', () => {\n594:   const cases = [\n595:     ['my agents md still has the old shipped sections and I want to know which ones are stale', '/doctor:agents-md check'],\n596:     ['embed the new shipped instructions into my agents md', '/doctor:agents-md embed'],\n597:     ['undo the agents md embed and bring back the file I had before', '/doctor:agents-md restore'],\n598:   ];\n599:   for (const [problem, runnable] of cases) {\n600:     const { status, report } = rank(problem);\n601:     assert.equal(status, 0, `${problem}: exit ${status}`);\n602:     assert.equal(report.status, 'match', problem);\n603:     assert.equal(report.candidates[0].runnable, runnable, `${problem} -> ${report.candidates[0].runnable}`);\n604:   }\n605: });\n606: \n607: test('every phrase on the three routes ranks its own route first', () => {\n608:   const { loadEntries, rankProblem } = require(HELPER);\n609:   const { entries } = loadEntries(path.resolve(DOCTOR, '..', '..', '..'));\n610:   const routable = entries.filter((entry) => entry.command !== '/doctor:helper');\n611:   const misses = [];\n612:   for (const route of ROUTES) {\n613:     const runnable = `/doctor:agents-md ${route.target}`;\n614:     assert.ok(routable.some((entry) => entry.runnable === runnable), `${runnable} has no helper entry`);\n615:     for (const phrase of route.trigger_phrases) {\n616:       const top = rankProblem(routable, phrase, {}).candidates[0];\n617:       if (!top || top.runnable !== runnable) misses.push(`\"${phrase}\" -> ${top ? top.runnable : 'no match'}`);\n618:     }\n619:   }\n620:   assert.deepEqual(misses, []);\n621: });\n622: \n623: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n624: // 8. THE LINES THE ENGINES PRINT AND THE FIELDS THAT CARRY THEM\n625: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n626: \n627: // A line an engine prints and neither the workflow keep-list nor the presentation names is\n628: // a line an agent can only drop, and a dropped pointer-sync line is a mirror reported as\n629: // verified when nothing wrote it.\n630: const embedRun = (args) => {\n631:   const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [EMBED_SCRIPT, ...args], { encoding: 'utf8', input: '' });\n632:   return { code: result.status, out: result.stdout || '', err: result.stderr || '' };\n633: };\n634: \n635: const printField = (text, name) => {\n636:   const match = new RegExp(`^${name}: (.*)$`, 'mu').exec(text);\n637:   return match === null ? null : match[1].trim();\n638: };\n639: \n640: // One composed repository per case, in a directory the case removes. Composition reads the\n641: // manifest, so a case describes the template that ships today rather than a stored copy.\n642: const composedTree = (t, name) => {\n643:   const parent = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), `doctor-agents-md-contract-${name}-`));\n644:   t.after(() => fs.rmSync(parent, { recursive: true, force: true }));\n645:   const dir = path.join(parent, name);\n646:   composeFixture(name, dir);\n647:   return dir;\n648: };\n649: \n650: // The engine never deletes a backup, so the case does: only the directory a run printed,\n651: // and only when it sits under the temporary directory it was created in.\n652: const trackBackup = (t, text) => {\n653:   for (const line of text.split('\\n')) {\n654:     const hit = /^backup: (\\S+)$/u.exec(line);\n655:     if (hit === null) continue;\n656:     const dir = hit[1];\n657:     t.after(() => {\n658:       if (!dir.startsWith(os.tmpdir() + path.sep)) return;\n659:       fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n660:     });\n661:   }\n662: };\n663: \n664: // The label of each field line an engine prints, read off its output rather than off its\n665: // source, so a line one of them gains arrives here as a failure with its own name. The\n666: // block body is skipped: its first word is the repository's, not the engine's.\n667: const printedLabels = (text) => {\n668:   const labels = new Set();\n669:   let inBlock = false;\n670:   for (const line of text.split('\\n')) {\n671:     if (line === 'block:') { inBlock = true; continue; }\n672:     if (line === 'block-end:') { inBlock = false; labels.add('block-end'); continue; }\n673:     if (inBlock) continue;\n674:     const hit = /^([a-z][a-z-]*)\\b/u.exec(line);\n675:     if (hit !== null) labels.add(hit[1]);\n676:   }\n677:   return labels;\n678: };\n679: \n680: // Where an operator meets each field line: the presentation's own field, and the phrase the\n681: // workflow keep-list uses. `note` and `finding` are pinned here too, though the fixtures\n682: // below happen not to print them, because the field has to exist for the run that does.\n683: const PRINTED_FIELDS = new Map([\n684:   ['target', { shown: /^Targets: /mu, kept: /the target list/u }],\n685:   ['note', { shown: /^Notes: /mu, kept: /each note/u }],\n686:   ['diff', { shown: /a `diff` per path/u, kept: /each diff/u }],\n687:   ['block', { shown: /^Block: /mu, kept: /`block:` and `block-end:`/u }],\n688:   ['block-end', { shown: /^Block: /mu, kept: /`block:` and `block-end:`/u }],\n689:   ['budget', { shown: /^Budget: /mu, kept: /the budget line/u }],\n690:   ['finding', { shown: /^Findings: /mu, kept: /each finding line/u }],\n691:   ['preservation', { shown: /^Preservation: /mu, kept: /the preservation line/u }],\n692:   ['backup', { shown: /^Backup folder: /mu, kept: /the backup line/u }],\n693:   ['backup-fallback', { shown: /^Backup note: /mu, kept: /the backup-fallback line/u }],\n694:   ['undo', { shown: /^Undo: /mu, kept: /the undo line/u }],\n695:   ['plan-digest', { shown: /^Plan digest: /mu, kept: /the plan-digest line/u }],\n696:   ['wrote', { shown: /^Files changed: /mu, kept: /one wrote or removed line per path/u }],\n697:   ['removed', { shown: /^Files changed: /mu, kept: /one wrote or removed line per path/u }],\n698:   ['pointer-sync', { shown: /^Pointer sync: /mu, kept: /the pointer-sync line/u }],\n699:   ['repo-rules', { shown: /^Router: /mu, kept: /the repo-rules line/u }],\n700:   ['check-after', { shown: /^Re-read: /mu, kept: /the check-after line/u }],\n701:   ['cp', { shown: /one copy line per overwritten file/u, kept: /one copy line per overwritten file/u }],\n702: ]);\n703: \n704: // The restore prints its own lines, so its plan and result templates are held to the same\n705: // rule: a folder a run created is a line an agent can only drop unless a field carries it.\n706: const RESTORE_FIELDS = new Map([\n707:   ['restore', { shown: /^Put back: /mu, kept: /one restore line per path/u }],\n708:   ['dry-run', { shown: /^Dry run: nothing was written and nothing was asked\\.$/mu, kept: /dry-run result/u }],\n709: ]);\n710: \n711: test('every field the writing engines print has a field in the presentation and a line in the keep-list', (t) => {\n712:   const dir = composedTree(t, 'claude-only');\n713:   const planned = embedRun(['plan', '--create-router', '--root', dir]);\n714:   trackBackup(t, planned.out);\n715:   assert.equal(planned.code, 0, planned.err);\n716:   const digest = printField(planned.out, 'plan-digest');\n717:   assert.match(digest || '', /^[0-9a-f]{64}$/u, 'the plan prints its digest');\n718: \n719:   const applied = embedRun(['apply', '--create-router', '--root', dir, '--plan-digest', digest]);\n720:   trackBackup(t, applied.out);\n721:   assert.equal(applied.code, 0, applied.err);\n722: \n723:   // The directory is named after the digest rather than after a clock reading, so the\n724:   // folder and the undo the operator approved are the ones apply used. A clock re-resolved\n725:   // at apply time named a directory no run ever created, and the approved undo exited 2.\n726:   assert.equal(printField(applied.out, 'backup'), printField(planned.out, 'backup'), 'apply backs up where the plan pointed');\n727:   assert.equal(printField(applied.out, 'undo'), printField(planned.out, 'undo'), 'the undo that was approved is the undo apply printed');\n728: \n729:   // The generator rewrites an existing pointer file and never creates a missing one, so a\n730:   // repository without one carries a nonzero verdict on a run that still ends STATUS=OK.\n731:   // That is the case the result template has to be able to show.\n732:   assert.match(applied.out, /^pointer-sync: exit 1 \\(.*skill-routing\\.md: missing/mu);\n733:   assert.doesNotMatch(applied.out, /wrote \\.cursor\\/rules\\/skill-routing\\.md/u);\n734: \n735:   const printed = [...printedLabels(planned.out), ...printedLabels(applied.out)];\n736:   const unnamed = [...new Set(printed)].filter((label) => !PRINTED_FIELDS.has(label)).sort();\n737:   assert.deepEqual(unnamed, [], 'an engine line no field carries');\n738: \n739:   const kept = `${phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan')}\\n${phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_4_write')}`;\n740:   for (const [label, where] of PRINTED_FIELDS) {\n741:     assert.ok(where.kept.test(kept), `${label}: the workflow keep-list does not name it`);\n742:     assert.ok(where.shown.test(PRESENTATION), `${label}: the presentation shows no field for it`);\n743:   }\n744: \n745:   // The restore templates carry the same obligation. The apply above created a .cursor\n746:   // folder for the mirror, so its plan prints the folder lines the result has to be able\n747:   // to show, and the run that removes them prints the other form of the same line.\n748:   const backup = printField(applied.out, 'backup');\n749:   const restorePlan = embedRun(['restore', `--run=${backup}`, '--root', dir, '--dry-run']);\n750:   assert.equal(restorePlan.code, 0, restorePlan.err);\n751:   assert.match(restorePlan.out, /^restore \\.cursor\\/rules\\/: remove if empty \\(this run created it\\)$/mu);\n752: \n753:   const restored = embedRun(['restore', `--run=${backup}`, '--root', dir, '--yes']);\n754:   assert.equal(restored.code, 0, restored.err);\n755:   assert.match(restored.out, /^restore \\.cursor\\/rules\\/: removed the empty folder this run created$/mu);\n756: \n757:   const restorePrinted = [...printedLabels(restorePlan.out), ...printedLabels(restored.out)];\n758:   const restoreUnnamed = [...new Set(restorePrinted)].filter((label) => !RESTORE_FIELDS.has(label)).sort();\n759:   assert.deepEqual(restoreUnnamed, [], 'a restore line no field carries');\n760: \n761:   const restoreKept = `${phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan')}\\n${phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_4_write')}`;\n762:   for (const [label, where] of RESTORE_FIELDS) {\n763:     assert.ok(where.kept.test(restoreKept), `${label}: the restore keep-list does not name it`);\n764:     assert.ok(where.shown.test(PRESENTATION), `${label}: the restore templates show no field for it`);\n765:   }\n766: \n767:   // A record names its own root, and a restore that runs against another one is refused,\n768:   // so the plan template, the result template and the route all name where that ends.\n769:   const refused = embedRun(['restore', `--run=${backup}`, '--yes']);\n770:   assert.equal(refused.code, 2, 'a restore against another root exits 2');\n771:   assert.match(refused.err, /ERROR: the record names the root .*pass --root/u);\n772:   const restorePlanTemplate = PRESENTATION.split('## 5. Restore Plan and Approval')[1].split(/\\n## 6\\./u)[0];\n773:   const restoredTemplate = PRESENTATION.split('### Restored')[1].split('### Failure Summary')[0];\n774:   assert.match(restorePlanTemplate, /^Folders: /mu, 'the plan template has no field for the folder lines');\n775:   assert.match(restoredTemplate, /^Folders: /mu, 'the result template has no field for the folder lines');\n776:   assert.match(restorePlanTemplate, /names another root/u);\n777:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^\\| A restore reports that the record names another root \\|/mu);\n778:   assert.match(phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan'), /names a root other than the one this restore runs against/u);\n779:   assert.match(phaseText(RESTORE_WORKFLOW, 'phase_4_write'), /names another root/u);\n780: });\n781: \n782: test('a plan on a repository with no router names the absent target and the backup note', (t) => {\n783:   const dir = composedTree(t, 'foreign');\n784:   const planned = embedRun(['plan', '--root', dir]);\n785:   assert.equal(planned.code, 0, planned.err);\n786: \n787:   // Two lines a plan prints that no field carried: the fifth target action, and the note\n788:   // that explains a backup placed outside the repository.\n789:   assert.match(planned.out, /^target REPO RULES\\.md: absent$/mu);\n790:   assert.match(planned.out, /^note: /mu);\n791:   assert.match(planned.out, /^backup-fallback: /mu);\n792: \n793:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /<create\\|replace\\|remove\\|unchanged\\|absent>/u);\n794:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /`absent` means the path is not there/u);\n795:   assert.match(PRESENTATION, /^Backup note: /mu);\n796:   const plan = phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_2_plan');\n797:   assert.match(plan, /absent/u);\n798:   assert.match(plan, /backup-fallback/u);\n799: });\n800: \n801: test('an embed whose pointer sync did not verify names the mirror it could not write', () => {\n802:   const embedded = PRESENTATION.split('### Embedded')[1].split('### Unchanged')[0];\n803:   for (const name of ['Pointer sync:', 'Router:', 'Next:']) {\n804:     assert.match(embedded, new RegExp(`^${name} `, 'mu'), `${name} is not a field of the result`);\n805:   }\n806: \n807:   const write = phaseText(EMBED_WORKFLOW, 'phase_4_write');\n808:   assert.match(write, /nonzero/u);\n809:   assert.match(write, /Next:.*\\/doctor:runtime-mirrors/u, 'a nonzero pointer sync names the mirror route as the next step');\n810:   assert.match(write, /never creates/u, 'the generator cannot create a missing pointer file');\n811:   assert.match(write, /Files changed/u, 'the file it cannot create is never listed as written');\n812: \n813:   // A repair for the row the re-read still reports, and a next step for the line that says\n814:   // why: the check route can only report that row again.\n815:   const troubleshooting = PRESENTATION.split('## 7. Troubleshooting Display')[1].split(/\\n## 8\\./u)[0];\n816:   const row = troubleshooting.split('\\n').find((line) => /^\\| `A10`/u.test(line));\n817:   assert.ok(row, 'the troubleshooting table has no A10 row');\n818:   assert.match(row, /\\/doctor:runtime-mirrors/u);\n819: \n820:   const nextRow = PRESENTATION.split('## 8. Next Step')[1].split('\\n').find((line) => /pointer-sync/u.test(line));\n821:   assert.ok(nextRow, 'the next-step table has no pointer-sync row');\n822:   assert.match(nextRow, /\\/doctor:runtime-mirrors/u);\n823: });"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794589286620,"end":1794589287414}}}}
