{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589402122,"sessionID":"ses_e2a25640effei5XE2iy7zBxs56","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5dd1bea002nIueDNm7mDC5iw","sessionID":"ses_e2a25640effei5XE2iy7zBxs56","messageID":"msg_1d5dd0e4c001eexJ9OYMQKHKjk","type":"tool","id":"call_27d0ba71e02e40fbb92cc3a9","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. When it holds ERROR: the restore failed, the restore itself threw and the tree may be partly written: quote both ERROR lines, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. This outcome takes precedence over the restored: outcome.\"","oldString":"      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\"","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml"},"output":"Edited .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml","patch":"Index: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n+++ .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n@@ -100,9 +100,9 @@\n       - \"Exit 2 with a message that the plan digest does not match the composition now means the tree changed after the plan, so nothing was written. Quote the engine's message, offer the plan again against the current tree, and end with STATUS=FAIL. Never retry the apply with a recomposed digest of your own: the point of the digest is that the approved bytes are the written bytes.\"\n       - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n       - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n       - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line or a `foreign:` line. The engine restored from the backup by itself unless it printed `nothing was restored`, and kept the backup. Quote the lines the proof named, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it when the restore ran. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n-      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\"\n+      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. When it holds ERROR: the restore failed, the restore itself threw and the tree may be partly written: quote both ERROR lines, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. This outcome takes precedence over the restored: outcome.\"\n       - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n \n   phase_5_reread:\n     purpose: \"Prove the written repository reads back through the read-only engine\"\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"      - \\\"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. When it holds ERROR: the restore failed, the restore itself threw and the tree may be partly written: quote both ERROR lines, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. This outcome takes precedence over the restored: outcome.\\\"\",\"oldString\":\"      - \\\"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\\\"\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794589400042,"end":1794589402122}}}}
