{"type":"text","timestamp":1794589447248,"sessionID":"ses_e2a25640effei5XE2iy7zBxs56","part":{"id":"prt_1d5ddcc8f002NHtZUoaXcif3m1","sessionID":"ses_e2a25640effei5XE2iy7zBxs56","messageID":"msg_1d5ddb940001aK8oO9FKsOWce6","type":"text","text":"T031 done. Two files changed, no checkbox ticked.\n\n**Files written**\n\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs` — added `test('the embed workflow reads a failed restore as a partly written tree')` in section 5. It finds the one `EMBED_YAML` line containing `Exit 3 means` and asserts the three patterns.\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml` — appended the restore-failure sentence inside the existing exit-3 quoted string on line 104.\n\n**Verify output**\n\nFirst `NT $DAC` run, before the YAML change (fails on the first pattern, as the task predicted):\n\n```\n✖ the embed workflow reads a failed restore as a partly written tree (0.319875ms)\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: The input did not match the regular expression /ERROR: the restore failed/. Input:\n  '      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. ... name the undo command as the next step.\"'\nℹ ticker... pass 37 / fail 1\n```\n\nAfter the YAML change, `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs`:\n\n```\nℹ tests 38\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 38\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 1304.024834\n```\n\n`bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` (RV): 18 `PASS:` lines, `OK: route-validate — 32 routes validated, 11 warnings`, `RV exit: 0`.\n\n`bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh`, exit 0, first two lines:\n\n```\nengine prints the restore failure: 1\nworkflow names the restore failure: 1\n```\n\n**Notes**\n\n- `git status` under `.skilled/commands/doctor` also shows `scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and `scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` modified. Those are lane WG9's files, not mine. My diff is confined to the two files named above.\n- The probe's remaining lines (`workflow backup name: doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/`, `route names the temporary-directory fallback: no`) are T032's targets, not T031's.\n- Nothing blocked. No spec folder docs written, no vitest suite run, no git mutation.","time":{"start":1794589445263,"end":1794589447248}}}
